    ('bitcoin:BTC', 'https://docs.google.com/document/d/13_eyEKvHbxVfyuMwN3HC9Ty8pPljMmHC6twwQYFoDt0/edit', $tank_seed_BTC_20261110$## BTC — Bitcoin: token & protocol fact sheet

As of 2026-11-10 (first pull ~14:30 UTC at chain tip 975,305–975,307; independently re-checked ~15:35 UTC at chain tip 975,315)

### Executive summary

BTC is the native asset of the Bitcoin network, a proof-of-work blockchain with a hard-coded maximum supply of 21,000,000 BTC, of which about 20.11 million (95.8%) has been issued as of block 975,305. Nothing in the protocol pays holders: all "protocol revenue" (block subsidy plus transaction fees, ~453 BTC/day ≈ $33.5M/day at $73,918) goes to miners as payment for security. Fees are only ~0.6–0.7% of miner income, so value comes entirely from demand for BTC as a scarce, censorship-resistant monetary asset, not from cash flows. The market is in a drawdown: BTC trades at $73,918 (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 15:33 UTC), -41.4% from its $126,080 all-time high (2025-10-06) and -29.5% year-on-year, with US spot ETFs posting net outflows in October (≈ -$515M per SimpleMining) and early November (≈ -$1.28B on Nov 2–6 per secondary trackers, not independently verified), while the largest corporate holder (Strategy, 850,364 BTC) is roughly at break-even versus its $75,456 average cost and sold ~$431.8M of BTC in 2026 (to 2026-10-25) to fund preferred dividends and STRC buybacks (company Q3 release). The single most important thing to watch is the marginal buyer: daily US spot-ETF flows plus Strategy's weekly 8-K buy/sell disclosures, because in 2026 these institutional channels (not on-chain usage) have set the price.

### What the token is

- Ticker: BTC (smallest unit: 1 satoshi = 0.00000001 BTC).

- Chain: native on the Bitcoin blockchain (UTXO model, SHA-256d proof-of-work). There is no contract address. Wrapped representations on other chains (e.g. WBTC, cbBTC, tBTC) are IOUs/bridged claims issued by third parties and are not BTC; they carry custodian/bridge risk.

- Launch: whitepaper published 2008-10-31 by pseudonymous Satoshi Nakamoto; genesis block 2009-01-03 ([whitepaper](https://bitcoin.org/bitcoin.pdf)).

- Monetary policy: block subsidy started at 50 BTC and halves every 210,000 blocks (~4 years). Current subsidy 3.125 BTC/block since the 4th halving (block 840,000, April 2024). Next halving at block 1,050,000 (subsidy → 1.5625 BTC), 74,695 blocks after the tip at 975,305: ~2028-04-12 at a 10-minute block time, ~2028-05-22 at the recent 646.7 s average (estimate, computed from [mempool.space difficulty-adjustment](https://mempool.space/api/v1/difficulty-adjustment)).

