### Revenue and value capture

Definitions for Bitcoin: (a) gross fees = transaction fees paid by users; (b) "protocol revenue" = everything the coinbase transaction pays to miners = subsidy + fees (the protocol itself keeps nothing, which is why DefiLlama reports Bitcoin revenue = $0); (c) value reaching token holders = zero direct cash flow. Holders bear the subsidy as dilution (~0.82%/yr). There are no buybacks, burns or distributions, and no fee switch is planned; changing this would contradict Bitcoin's design and has no proposal with traction.

