Why it matters: fees are only ~0.6–0.7% of miner income (21shares measured 0.67% for Q3 2026). The mempool is nearly empty at the top: recommended fee 4 sat/vB "fastest", 1 sat/vB minimum (15:35 UTC; 5 sat/vB fastest at 14:30 UTC), and ~30.8 of ~32.6 MvB waiting in the mempool pays below 1 sat/vB, mostly ~0.1 sat/vB (Core's lowered minimum relay fee) ([mempool.space fees](https://mempool.space/api/v1/fees/recommended)). Each halving cuts the subsidy by 50%; 21shares estimates the 2028 halving at September-2026 prices would leave rewards covering ~80% of miners' power costs. The long-run "security budget" question (fees replacing subsidy) is unresolved and is a structural, not near-term, risk.

Mechanism (exact): there is no fee-collector contract. Each block's first transaction (coinbase) creates outputs to addresses chosen by the miner/pool; consensus permits these outputs to total at most subsidy + fees of that block (e.g. block 975,305 mined by F2Pool: subsidy 312,500,000 sat + fees 7,109,161 sat = 319,609,161 sat, 3,528 tx, median fee 6.0 sat/vB). Underclaimed amounts are destroyed forever.

### How to verify on-chain

All numbers below were first obtained on 2026-11-10 between ~14:25 and ~14:40 UTC and every command was re-run independently at ~15:35 UTC (re-run values shown where they moved). No API keys are needed for these endpoints.

#### 1. Chain tip, difficulty, size (public JSON-RPC)

curl -s -H 'content-type: application/json' \  -d '{"jsonrpc":"1.0","id":1,"method":"getblockchaininfo","params":[]}' \  https://bitcoin-rpc.publicnode.com

Obtained: blocks 975,307 (14:35 UTC); re-run: blocks 975,315, difficulty 148,364,561,003,867.4, size_on_disk 891,656,583,179 bytes.

#### 2. Subsidy and fees of a specific block

curl -s -H 'content-type: application/json' \  -d '{"jsonrpc":"1.0","id":1,"method":"getblockstats","params":[975305,["height","subsidy","totalfee","txs","avgfeerate"]]}' \  https://bitcoin-rpc.publicnode.com

Obtained (identical on re-run): subsidy 312,500,000 sat (3.125 BTC), totalfee 7,109,161 sat, 3,528 tx, avgfeerate 7 sat/vB. Cross-check via mempool.space: curl -s https://mempool.space/api/v1/block/$(curl -s https://mempool.space/api/block-height/975305) → reward 319,609,161 sat, pool F2Pool.

#### 3. Miner revenue and fees over N blocks

curl -s https://mempool.space/api/v1/mining/reward-stats/144    # ~1 daycurl -s https://mempool.space/api/v1/mining/reward-stats/1008   # ~1 weekcurl -s https://mempool.space/api/v1/mining/reward-stats/4320   # ~1 month

Obtained (sat, 14:30 UTC, end block 975,305): 144 → totalReward 45,317,501,882 / totalFee 317,501,882; 1008 → 317,245,756,251 / 2,245,756,251; 4320 → 1,357,812,332,687 / 7,812,332,687. Re-run (15:35 UTC, end block 975,315): 144 → 45,324,432,006 / 324,432,006; 1008 → 317,261,169,727 / 2,261,169,727; 4320 → 1,357,826,043,540 / 7,826,043,540.

#### 4. Supply

curl -s https://api.blockchain.info/stats   # field "totalbc" = satoshis issued (theoretical), "n_blocks_total"# exact UTXO-set supply from your own node (slow, minutes):bitcoin-cli gettxoutsetinfo muhash   # field "total_amount"

Obtained: api.blockchain.info/stats totalbc = 2,011,033,125,000,000 sat (20,110,331.25 BTC), identical to the subsidy-schedule sum at height 975,305; re-run: totalbc 2,011,036,250,000,000 sat at n_blocks_total 975,316 (= sum through height 975,315). Note: the shorter endpoint https://blockchain.info/q/totalbc returned 2,011,032,800,000,000 sat at the same moment, which is not a whole number of 3.125-BTC subsidies (stale/rounded cache), so use /stats instead. gettxoutsetinfo total_amount will be slightly lower (genesis 50 BTC unspendable, underclaimed coinbases, provably unspendable outputs); not run here because public RPCs do not serve it.

#### 5. Hashrate, difficulty adjustment, pool concentration, fees, mempool

curl -s https://mempool.space/api/v1/mining/hashrate/1mcurl -s https://mempool.space/api/v1/difficulty-adjustmentcurl -s https://mempool.space/api/v1/mining/pools/1wcurl -s https://mempool.space/api/v1/fees/recommendedcurl -s https://mempool.space/api/mempool

