#### 7. Large-holder checks

- Strategy: weekly 8-K filings on [SEC EDGAR (CIK 1050446)](https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001050446&type=8-K); Strategy also publishes holdings on strategy.com. Its wallet addresses are not fully disclosed, so on-chain verification is not possible from public data.

- ETFs: issuers publish daily holdings, e.g. the [iShares IBIT page](https://www.ishares.com/us/products/333011/ishares-bitcoin-trust-etf) (2026-11-09: net assets $59,498,784,461; 1,406,320,000 shares; basket 22.64 BTC per 40,000 shares → ≈795,900 BTC). Several ETFs disclose custody addresses through Arkham-type labelling only; flows are tracked by Farside/SoSoValue (Farside blocked automated fetch on 2026-11-10).

- Release integrity: Bitcoin Core release signers/maintainer keys are in [contrib/verify-commits/trusted-keys](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/master/contrib/verify-commits/trusted-keys) (5 fingerprints on 2026-11-10).

### Key people

Bitcoin has no CEO, foundation or DAO. "Key actors" are the people and institutions who write the software, produce blocks, and hold or wrap large amounts of BTC.

| Actor | Role | Notes |

| --- | --- | --- |

| Satoshi Nakamoto | Pseudonymous creator (2008–2010) | Inactive since ~2011; attributed ~1.1M BTC (estimate) never moved. |

| Bitcoin Core maintainers (merge keys) | Merge code into the reference implementation; do not control consensus | 5 trusted keys on 2026-11-10: Michael Ford (fanquake), Hennadii Stepanov (hebasto), Ava Chow (achow101), Ryan Ofsky (ryanofsky), "sedited" = Sebastian Kung / TheCharlatan (added 2026-01-08, first key added since ryanofsky in 2023-05). Fingerprint-to-name mapping re-checked against the keys' published PGP user IDs (keys.openpgp.org). Departures: Gloria Zhao (removed 2025-09-18), Marco Falke (2023), Wladimir van der Laan (2023). Project X: [@bitcoincoreorg](https://x.com/bitcoincoreorg). |

| Bitcoin Knots (Luke Dashjr) | Alternative node implementation with stricter data/spam policy | Shipped BIP-110 enforcement; ~20% of reachable nodes (Aug 2026 count). X: [@LukeDashjr](https://x.com/LukeDashjr). |

| BIP-360 authors: Hunter Beast, Ethan Heilman, Isabel Foxen Duke | Quantum-resistant output type (P2MR) proposal | Merged into BIPs repo Feb 2026 as a draft; not activated. |

| Developer funders | Brink, Chaincode Labs, Spiral (Block), OpenSats, HRF | Fund most Core contributors via grants/employment. |

| Mining pools | Block production / transaction selection | Foundry USA (DCG), AntPool (Bitmain), F2Pool, ViaBTC, SpiderPool, MARA, OCEAN, Luxor, Braiins. Top 3 ≈ 61% of blocks in the last week. |

| Strategy Inc | Largest corporate holder (850,364 BTC) | Michael Saylor, Founder & Executive Chairman ([@saylor](https://x.com/saylor)); Phong Le, President & CEO, also principal financial officer 2026-11-06 to 2026-12-31; Andrew Kang stepped down as EVP & CFO effective 2026-11-05 (stays as adviser); Reza Virasteh (EVP Operations) becomes EVP & CFO on 2027-01-01; Shelley Khanna becomes chief accounting officer 2026-11-06 ([Q3 release](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001050446/000105044626000047/mstr-20261029x8kxex9912.htm), primary; [BitcoinTreasuries](https://bitcointreasuries.net/news/strategy-reports-record-dollar21-billion-q3-operating-income-as-cfo-steps-down)). |

| ETF issuers | Largest custodial holders | BlackRock IBIT ($59.50B net assets, ≈795,900 BTC, 2026-11-09, [iShares](https://www.ishares.com/us/products/333011/ishares-bitcoin-trust-etf); an earlier report cited ~$66.1B on 2026-10-28, unverified), Fidelity FBTC (~$14.3B) and Grayscale GBTC (~$10.2B) as of 2026-10-28 per secondary reports (unverified). Custody largely at Coinbase. |

| US government | Holder/regulator | Strategic Bitcoin Reserve by executive order signed 2025-03-06 (funded with forfeited BTC; the US will not sell those coins; only budget-neutral acquisition allowed) ([Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Strategic_Bitcoin_Reserve)). Sen. Cynthia Lummis sponsored the BITCOIN Act (1M BTC purchase over five years; reintroduced 2025-03-11, not passed). A reported House Financial Services vote advancing the "American Reserve Modernization Act" 28–21 on 2026-09-16 could not be confirmed in the cited source (unverified). |

| Mt. Gox trustee Nobuaki Kobayashi | Controls ~34.4k BTC estate | Repayment deadline extended from 2026-10-31 to 2027-10-31 (trustee notice 2026-10-16, reported 2026-10-20). |

### Recent news (last ~90 days)

- 2026-08-04 — Russia: Putin signs law bringing crypto trading under central-bank licensing; on 2026-08-11 the Bank of Russia approved BTC, ETH and USDT for exchange trading with retail caps ([IntelliNews](https://www.intellinews.com/putin-signs-law-bringing-russia-s-crypto-market-under-central-bank-licensing-458991/), [Meduza](https://meduza.io/en/news/2026/08/11/russia-s-central-bank-approves-bitcoin-ethereum-and-usdt-for-exchange-trading-with-limits-for-retail-investors)).

- 2026-08-08 — BIP-110 ("Reduced Data Temporary Softfork") mandatory signalling began at block 961,632; only 2.53% of blocks had signalled (55% needed). Enforcing Knots nodes split onto a minority chain that mined two blocks and stalled (~99.85% of hashrate stayed on Bitcoin). The project later moved its chain to BLAKE2b PoW; no major exchange listed it ([Mining Disrupt](https://miningdisrupt.com/bips/110), [Jimmy Song](https://jimmysong.substack.com/p/the-messy-middle-or-what-actually)).

- Aug 2026 — BTC +~25% in August (from ~$63k early month to ~$79–81k); spot ETFs +$3.52B, best month of 2026; nine straight inflow days Aug 17–27 ([Cointelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-etf-best-month-2026-btc-up-25-august)).

- Jul–Aug 2026 — Strategy sold 5,553 BTC ($349M) to fund preferred dividends/STRC repurchases, then bought 7,128 BTC from late August ([21shares](https://www.21shares.com/en-us/insights/bitcoin-etf-inflows-q3-2026)).

- 2026-09-14 — Bitcoin Core 32.0 release-candidate cycle started (v32.0rc1; target release 2026-10-10) ([crypto.news](https://crypto.news/bitcoin-core-32-enters-final-testing-ahead-of-release/)). Per the official 32.1 release notes, "due to last-minute issues, 32.0, although tagged, was never fully announced or released" ([release-notes-32.1.md](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/master/doc/release-notes/release-notes-32.1.md)).

- 2026-09-15 — CLARITY Act (US market-structure bill) failed Senate cloture 49–50; expires with the Congress on 2027-01-03 unless revived ([DLA Piper](https://www.dlapiper.com/en/insights/publications/2026/09/senate-fails-to-advance-the-clarity-act), [Orrick](https://www.orrick.com/en/Insights/2026/10/The-CLARITY-Act-Stalls-in-the-Senate-Whats-Next-for-Digital-Asset-Regulation)).

- 2026-09-16 (unverified) — Reported: House Financial Services advanced the American Reserve Modernization Act (formal Treasury custody of reserve BTC, 20-year hold, proof of reserves; no 1M BTC purchase target) 28–21. The cited Wikipedia article did not contain this on re-check; treat as unconfirmed.

- 2026-09-21 to 25 — ETFs +$2.4B in a week (largest since Oct 2025), flipping 2026 YTD flows positive; Sept 21 +$999M was 2026's largest day ([The Block](https://www.theblock.co/news/markets/2026-09-26-bitcoin-etfs-turn-positive-for-2026-with-2-4-billion-weekly-inflow-their-largest-since-october-416944)). Q3 closed at ~$83,570 (+42.7% q/q).

- 2026-10-12 — Binance issued a notice discontinuing Binance Pool, Pool Savings, Cloud Mining and Transaction Accelerator on 2026-11-10; Binance Pool had mined 22,188 blocks and 137,059 BTC since 2020-04-24 ([Bitcoin.com](https://news.bitcoin.com/binance-pulls-plug-bitcoin-mining-after-6-year-run/)).

- Oct 2026 — BTC -7.34% for October (weakest October 2015–2026 per one report); ETFs ≈ -$515M net; IBIT +$665M on 2026-10-19 (largest day since Oct 2025) ([SimpleMining](https://www.simplemining.io/insights/post/bitcoin-market-report-october-2026), [The Block](https://www.theblock.co/news/markets/2026-10-20-blackrock-ibit-bitcoin-etf-665-million-421102)). Mid-October hot CPI; a December Fed hike priced ~95% at the time ([Nexo](https://nexo.com/blog/markets-today-october-14)).

- 2026-10-16/20 — Mt. Gox repayment deadline extended a sixth time, to 2027-10-31; ~34.4k BTC remain in estate wallets ([Cointelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/news/mt-gox-creditor-repayment-deadline-extended-2027)).

- 2026-10-27/28 — Bitcoin Core 32.1 released (first public 32.x), plus 31.2, 30.4, 29.5; three CVEs disclosed on 2026-10-28 (CVE-2026-117349 memory growth from paused pre-BIP31 peers; CVE-2026-117350 TCP urgent-data OOM on non-Linux; CVE-2026-117346 undo-file overflow under extreme reorg conditions). The 32.1 notes declare 29.x and older end-of-life and pre-announce disclosure of 3 medium/high-severity vulnerabilities fixed in 30.0 two weeks after release ([bitcoincore.org](https://bitcoincore.org/en/2026/10/27/release-32.1/), [blog](https://bitcoincore.org/en/blog/)).

- 2026-10-29 — Strategy Q3: 848,517 BTC (Oct 25), $20.91B gain on digital assets, $19.12B net income; $2.04B of STRC repurchases; USD assets $5.07B (3.4 years of dividend/interest coverage); YTD "BTC yield" -3.7%; ~$431.8M of BTC sold YTD; CFO Andrew Kang stepping down effective 2026-11-05 ([SEC exhibit 99.1](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001050446/000105044626000047/mstr-20261029x8kxex9912.htm)).

- 2026-11-02 — Strategy 8-K: bought 811 BTC ($65.5M, avg $80,846) Oct 26–Nov 1; holdings 849,327 BTC ([SEC](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001050446/000119312526442707/mstr-20261102.htm)).

- 2026-11-03/04 — US midterms: Democrats won control of both House and Senate ([Bankless](https://www.bankless.com/read/news/crypto-holds-steady-as-democrats-sweep-congress), 2026-11-04); BTC briefly sank to ~$75.7k overnight, then recovered to ~$79.3k; CoinGecko hourly data show a 2026-11-04 high of ~$80.7k.

- 2026-11-05 — BTC fell as much as 5.8% to below $76,000 as the Nasdaq-100 dropped 6.4% ([Bloomberg](https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-05/bitcoin-sinks-to-seven-week-low-as-risk-off-mood-deepens), paywalled/bot-blocked on re-check; CoinGecko hourly low that day ~$75,663 is consistent); US spot ETFs ≈ -$1.28B net Nov 2–6 (secondary trackers).

- 2026-11-09 — Strategy 8-K: bought 1,036 BTC ($81.9M, avg $79,012) Nov 2–8; holdings 850,364 BTC at $75,456 average; also repurchased $188.3M of STRC ([SEC](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001050446/000119312526452693/mstr-20261109.htm)).

- 2026-11-10 — BTC $73,918 (CoinGecko 15:33 UTC), -11.0% over 30 days; Binance Pool discontinued; US October CPI release scheduled (date as reported; BLS schedule page blocked automated fetch).

### Current problems and risks

- Price drawdown and weak demand: -41.4% from ATH, -29.5% y/y (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 15:33 UTC); 2026 low ~$58,244 on 2026-06-25 14:00 UTC in CoinGecko hourly data (daily-snapshot low $58,566 on 2026-07-01 00:00 UTC), after an intraday drop to near $60,000 on 2026-02-06 ([Backpack](https://learn.backpack.exchange/articles/bitcoin-crash); CoinGecko hourly low that day $62,778). Demand depends heavily on ETF flows, which reversed to outflows in Oct–Nov.

- Treasury-company reflexivity: Strategy is roughly at break-even (850,364 BTC × $73,918 ≈ $62.9B vs $64.16B cost), finances itself via MSTR equity sales and preferred stock with cash dividends ($419.6M preferred dividends in Q3), and sold ~$431.8M of BTC in 2026 to 2026-10-25. Most large DATs trade near or below mNAV 1 (secondary reports), limiting their ability to raise capital to buy BTC.

- Miner economics and security budget: fees are ~0.6–0.7% of miner revenue; hashprice ~$33–38/PH/day; hashrate down from ~1.3 ZH/s peak; next difficulty retarget estimated -6.9% to -7.2%; miners pivoting to AI; pools shutting (Binance). Hash concentration: top 3 pools ≈ 61% of blocks.

- Governance friction: Core vs Knots dispute over OP_RETURN/data policy produced a (failed) chain split in August 2026; ~20% of reachable nodes run Knots. Not a threat to the main chain so far, but a signal of community division.

- Quantum computing: ECDSA/Schnorr keys are vulnerable to a sufficiently large quantum computer; a March-2026 Google paper (as reported; not re-verified, Forbes page blocked automated fetch) lowered estimated requirements to <500,000 physical qubits; an estimated ~1/3 of BTC sits in outputs with exposed public keys (single-study estimate, unverified). BIP-360 (P2MR) and BIP-361 (migration) are drafts only; no activation path agreed.

- Software security: three Bitcoin Core CVEs disclosed 2026-10-28 (fixed in 29.5/30.4/31.2/32.1); a 2026-06 private-broadcast IP-leak disclosure.

- US policy: CLARITY Act stalled (49–50); the new Democratic Congress (from Jan 2027) plans changes. BTC itself is treated as a commodity, so direct risk is moderate, but crypto-market structure, bank access and ETF-adjacent rules could shift. The SBR has no statutory basis yet and has bought nothing.

- Macro: rate-hike expectations (December FOMC), high Treasury yields (>4.8% cited in Sept), and correlation with the Nasdaq/AI trade.

- Legacy overhangs: Mt. Gox (~34.4k BTC, by Oct 2027), government-held coins, early-whale distribution (LTH -248k BTC in Q3).

What the market still believes in (bull case cited by participants): ETFs absorbed ~2× new issuance in Q3; sovereign adoption is spreading (US reserve legislation, Russia retail access); Strategy's Saylor said "We're at the beginning of the next bitcoin bull market" and that BTC was 21% above its 200-week moving average (Q3 press release, 2026-10-29); supply issuance halves again in ~2028.

