    ('ethereum:ETH', 'https://docs.google.com/document/d/1196hJIlVnvvr5CnvN99K85w5QwiNBSOGRQyAOVZXSFk/edit', $tank_seed_ETH_20261110$## ETH — Ethereum: token & protocol fact sheet

As of 2026-11-10. Live numbers were pulled between 14:30 and 14:45 UTC on 2026-11-10 unless another date is given. Ethereum block height at that time was about 26,385,130 and beacon slot about 15,624,760. Prices are in USD. "Fees", "revenue" and "holders revenue" follow DefiLlama's definitions unless stated otherwise. Bracketed numbers such as [1] refer to the Sources section. An independent fact-check re-queried the key figures between 15:39 and 15:50 UTC on 2026-11-10; where values moved, the fresher value and time are shown (see Verification notes).

### Executive summary

ETH is the native asset of Ethereum, the largest smart-contract blockchain by DeFi TVL and stablecoin float. There is no company behind it. A Swiss non-profit, the Ethereum Foundation (EF), funds research, and about a dozen independent client teams maintain the software. ETH pays for gas, is the only asset that can be staked to secure proof-of-stake consensus, and is the main collateral asset of Ethereum DeFi. Today almost no fee value reaches holders. Users paid $20.05M in L1 fees over the last 30 days. Only $6.21M (2,727 ETH) of that was burned, while new issuance to stakers ran at about 89,500 ETH over the same 30 days. The supply is therefore inflating at about +0.86% a year. The burn is equivalent to about 0.03% of market cap a year. Stakers earn about 2.46% APR, almost entirely from new issuance, so staking mostly offsets dilution rather than paying out real yield. The current state is weak. ETH is $2,036.88 (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 15:39 UTC), down 42.5% year on year and 58.8% below its 2025-08-24 all-time high of $4,946. US spot ETFs have been in net outflow since early October: a record 23-day outflow streak ended 2026-10-30, followed by −$365.2M over 2–6 November and −$184.5M on 2026-11-09. The largest corporate buyer, BitMine, is about 40k ETH short of its self-imposed 5% hard cap. The EF has lost both co-executive directors in 2026 and faces a lawsuit. The next upgrade, Glamsterdam, is delayed with no mainnet date. Vitalik Buterin said on 2026-11-08 that the investment case should rest on ETH as a "store of value", not on fee burn. Single most important thing to watch: net marginal demand once BitMine's buying stops, meaning whether ETF and treasury flows turn positive or the staking entry queue (currently 904k ETH) drains. Fee revenue is too small to set the price.

### What the token is

- Ticker / type: ETH. ETH is the native coin of Ethereum mainnet (chain ID 1), not a contract token. It has no contract address. Balances live in the account state, and on the consensus layer they live in validator balances.

- Wrapped and bridged forms (not ETH itself): WETH on mainnet is 0xC02aaA39b223FE8D0A0e5C4F27eAD9083C756Cc2 and held 2,098,356 ETH on 2026-11-10 15:4x UTC (eth_getBalance, own read; 2,102,909 ETH at 14:3x UTC). ETH bridged to rollups sits in L1 bridge contracts. The Arbitrum One bridge 0x8315177aB297bA92A06054cE80a67Ed4DBd7ed3a held 755,400 ETH and the Base OptimismPortal 0x49048044D57e1C92A77f79988d21Fa8fAF74E97e held 855,943 ETH (own reads, 2026-11-10 15:4x UTC; contract types confirmed on Etherscan as TransparentUpgradeableProxy and Proxy respectively). ETH is also the gas token on most Ethereum L2s: Base, Arbitrum, OP Mainnet and others.

- Supply: there is no maximum supply. Supply is set by protocol issuance to validators minus the EIP-1559 burn.

