- Issuance schedule: issuance is not fixed by time. It is a function of total staked ETH and is roughly proportional to √(total stake). The current estimate is 0.4155 ETH per 12-second slot, or about 1.09M ETH a year (~0.89%) (ultrasound.money issuance-estimate and gauge-rates, 2026-11-10 [3]). Annualized burn on the 30-day average is 33,201 ETH, so net supply growth is +0.864% a year (30-day basis) or +0.886% a year (1-day basis) [3]. For comparison, ultrasound.money estimates that the PoW-era issuance would have been 4.93M ETH a year.

- Unlocks: none. No vesting schedules or team or VC cliffs exist. The 2014 crowdsale and genesis allocations are fully liquid. The closest equivalent to an "unlock" is the validator exit queue, which was 5,061 ETH with a 1.1-day wait on 2026-11-09 [5]. Its all-time high in the validatorqueue.com series was 2.68M ETH on 2025-09-12 (it was still 2.46M ETH, 42.6-day wait, on 2025-11-01). In 2026 it peaked at 652k ETH on 2026-05-02, and it jumped from 200k to 567k ETH between 2026-09-30 and 2026-10-01 after the MetaMask Staking incident [5][24].

