### The protocol/business

Ethereum is a general-purpose settlement layer. Its "product lines" are:

- L1 blockspace for high-value DeFi, stablecoin and RWA settlement.

- Data availability (blobs) for rollups.

- Staking, which is the security service.

Its users are DeFi protocols, stablecoin issuers (Tether, Circle, Sky, Ethena), tokenization platforms, L2 operators (Coinbase/Base, Offchain Labs/Arbitrum, Optimism, Robinhood Chain), institutions via ETFs and custodians, and retail via exchanges and wallets. Activity is global. Retail flow increasingly happens on L2s, while L1 serves high-value transactions. On-chain metrics cannot reliably identify regions. Institutional ETH exposure is concentrated in US ETFs and US-listed treasury companies.

