As of 2026-11-10

On-chain values were read on 2026-11-10 at about 14:33 UTC (Ethereum block 26,385,133) and re-read by an independent fact-checker at 15:42 UTC (block 26,385,478); where they differ, the 15:42 UTC value is shown. "DL" means DefiLlama and "CG" means CoinGecko. USD values of UNI burns are priced at the CoinGecko daily UNI/USD close for the day of each burn.

### Executive summary

UNI is the governance token of the Uniswap protocol, the largest on-chain spot DEX. Uniswap processed about $63.2B in volume over the last 30 days, roughly 25–28% of tracked DEX volume. Since the "UNIfication" proposal passed in December 2025, value does reach holders. It arrives as a programmatic burn, not as dividends. Protocol fees from v2, v3 and (since July 2026) v4 pools collect in on-chain "TokenJar" contracts. Anyone can withdraw them by burning UNI through a "Firepit" contract. From 2025-12-29 to 2026-11-10 15:40 UTC this burned 13.90M UNI, about $64.3M at the time of each burn. That figure matches DefiLlama's holder-revenue figure of $64.0M almost exactly. The current pace is about $8.3M per 30 days, about $100M a year at the 30-day rate. On top of that, a one-off 100M UNI was burned from the treasury on 2025-12-27. The protocol is healthy and growing in features, but recent fees are heavily concentrated in speculative Robinhood Chain flow: 37% of the last 30 days' LP fees. Burns peaked in September 2026 ($17.8M) and have since halved, and UNI has fallen from about $10.2 (2026-09-23 daily close) to $6.87 (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 15:42 UTC). The single most important thing to watch is the monthly burn run-rate (USD and UNI) against the 20M UNI/year growth budget paid out of the treasury to Uniswap Labs. At today's price the growth budget is about $137M a year, more than the current annualized burn (about $99–101M).

### What the token is

- Ticker / name: UNI, Uniswap. ERC-20 token deployed 2020-09-16 by Uniswap Labs. It has governance (Compound-style GovernorBravo) and a capped inflation feature.

- Canonical contract (Ethereum): 0x1f9840a85d5aF5bf1D1762F925BDADdC4201F984 (verified: totalSupply() returns 1,000,000,000 UNI).

- Bridged representations (per CoinGecko platform list and Uniswap docs): Arbitrum 0xfa7f8980b0f1e64a2062791cc3b0871572f1f7f0; OP Mainnet 0x6fd9d7ad17242c41f7131d257212c54a0e816691; Polygon 0xb33eaad8d922b1083446dc23f610c2567fb5180f; BNB Chain 0xbf5140a22578168fd562dccf235e5d43a02ce9b1; Unichain 0x8f187aa05619a017077f5308904739877ce9ea21; Avalanche 0x8ebaf22b6f053dffeaf46f4dd9efa95d89ba8580; Gnosis 0x4537e328bf7e4efa29d05caea260d7fe26af9d74. For burn routing, the Uniswap docs also list a Wormhole NTT "SyntheticNttUni" 0x06e8bdE95BE4ce5cB1134BD47aD18a79fFB35822 on BNB Chain and Polygon. All bridged UNI is ultimately backed by the Ethereum token.

