Uniswap's holder take of about 10.5% of LP fees ($8.13M / $77.5M) is far below Aero's (about 72%). This is by design: the fee switch takes only 1/6–1/4 of LP fees on fee-enabled pools.

### Revenue and value capture

(a) Gross fees paid by users are the LP fees. (b) Protocol revenue is the slice diverted to the TokenJars. (c) Value to holders is UNI burned via the Firepits; the mechanism routes 100% of (b) to (c). Unichain sequencer fees, net of L1 costs and Optimism's 15%, are also routed to the burn but are negligible: DL shows $770 of Unichain holders revenue over 30 days and $112.8K over 1 year. Uniswap Labs' own interface fees are zero (DL "Uniswap Labs" fees: $0 over 30 days, versus $4.16M over 1 year before the switch-off).

| Period (DL: complete UTC days to 2026-11-09; on-chain: to 2026-11-10 15:40 UTC) | (a) Fees, DL | (b)=(c) Revenue / holders revenue, DL | (c) UNI burned on-chain (author, Etherscan logs) | (c) USD value of on-chain burns |

