    ('pancakeswap:CAKE', 'https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HY6iwRBt_uBM0mMskm_mV_2SlLhtiT0JBFwCLvtunjs/edit', $tank_seed_CAKE_20261110$## CAKE — PancakeSwap: token & protocol fact sheet

As of 2026-11-10. Data pulls were made 2026-11-10 between 14:30 and 16:10 UTC unless stated otherwise (market, TVL and DEX-share figures were re-pulled by an independent fact-check at 15:50–16:10 UTC). "On-chain" means a direct read through the public BNB Smart Chain RPC (bsc-rpc.publicnode.com) that I ran myself. "DefiLlama" means api.llama.fi. "Burn dashboard" means PancakeSwap's own data feed at burn-stats.pancakeswap.com/data.json, which powers [pancakeswap.finance/burn-dashboard](https://pancakeswap.finance/burn-dashboard).

### Executive summary

CAKE is the native token of PancakeSwap. PancakeSwap is a multichain AMM DEX run by an anonymous team ("the Kitchen"); about 97% of its TVL and about 94% of its fees are on BNB Chain. CAKE has no fee share, no staking yield and no gas role. Holders get value only through supply reduction: part of every swap fee buys CAKE on the open market and burns it, while new emissions have been cut to about 21.7k CAKE/day (I confirmed this rate on-chain). Burns do reach holders today. In the 4 burn weeks to 2026-11-02, 1.54M CAKE (about $3.3M) was bought and burned. October net supply fell 1.12M CAKE (−0.34%), the 38th consecutive month of net deflation. The business has shrunk sharply, though. Monthly volume fell from $110B (Oct 2025) to $24B (Oct 2026), 30-day fees are about $10.6M, and the price is $1.81 (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 15:51 UTC), −27% YoY and −96% from ATH. The most important thing to watch is the rollout of "The Flip". It passed on 2026-10-24, with one wallet casting 99% of the "For" votes. It moves the v3/Infinity protocol share (≈48% of recent buyback-burns) from the burn to the Treasury (the proposal says the non-stablecoin part will still buy back CAKE, but does not commit to burning it) and steps emissions down to 11k and then 7k CAKE/day. The rollout started on Robinhood Chain in early Nov 2026; BNB Chain switches last. The weekly buyback-burn due 2026-11-09 was postponed to 2026-11-16 for a security upgrade of the buyback contracts. Whether the burn-versus-emission balance holds as BNB Chain v3 switches, together with whether BNB Chain DEX volume recovers, will decide whether CAKE stays deflationary.

### What the token is

- Ticker / name: CAKE, "PancakeSwap Token" (on-chain name() on BSC returns "PancakeSwap Token"). CoinGecko id pancakeswap-token, market-cap rank #96.

- Canonical contract (BNB Smart Chain, BEP-20): 0x0E09FaBB73Bd3Ade0a17ECC321fD13a19e81cE82. The minting owner is MasterChef v1 0x73feaa1eE314F8c655E354234017bE2193C9E24E, verified on-chain via owner(). The token contract has no hard-coded cap. The "400M max supply" is a governance policy. It is not a contract constraint.

- Bridged deployments (LayerZero OFT; addresses from CoinGecko, supplies read on-chain where noted): Ethereum 0x152649eA73beAb28c5b49B26eb48f7EAD6d4c898 (totalSupply 5,309,284 CAKE, on-chain); Base 0x3055913c90Fcc1A6CE9a358911721eEb942013A1 (468,534 CAKE, on-chain); Arbitrum 0x1b896893dfc86bb67Cf57767298b9073D2c1bA2c (145,256 CAKE, on-chain); opBNB 0x2779106e4F4A8A28d77A24c18283651a2AE22D1C; zkSync Era 0x3A287a06c66f9E95a56327185cA2BDF5f031cEcD; Linea and Polygon zkEVM 0x0D1E753a25eBda689453309112904807625bEFBe; Aptos 0x159df6b7…::oft::CakeOFT; Solana 4qQeZ5LwSz6HuupUu8jCtgXyW1mYQcNbFAW1sWZp89HL. Bridged CAKE is a representation of BSC CAKE and does not add supply. CAKE bridging out of opBNB via LayerZero ends 2026-11-23 00:00 UTC ([Kitchen Report Oct 2026](https://blog.pancakeswap.finance/articles/kitchen-report-october-2026)).

