Caution on mid-week snapshots: the burn dashboard JSON at 2026-11-10 01:07 UTC showed total_supply 388.5M. Emission "mint-and-burn" CAKE builds up in a burn multisig and is burned in a weekly batch, so the dashboard's supply line jumps by about 50–60M between batches. Use the post-burn weekly close, or the computation above.

#### Emission schedule (no vesting, no VC unlocks)

- CAKE launched in Sep 2020 with no presale and no team or investor vesting tranches. New supply enters only through emissions. There are no scheduled unlock cliffs. The supply risk is emission policy, not unlocks.

- Mechanics, verified on-chain: MasterChef v1 still mints 40 CAKE per BSC block (cakePerBlock()). MasterChef v2 (0xa5f8C5Dbd5F286960b9d90548680aE5ebFf07652) routes cakeRateToBurn = 99.7168% of that to the burn admin, which burns it, and only cakeRateToSpecialFarm = 0.2832% is kept. cakePerBlock(false) = 0.11329 CAKE/block. At the measured 0.450 s block time (10,000 blocks = 4,501 s), that is ≈21,747 CAKE/day ≈ 7.94M CAKE/yr. This matches the official October mint of 674,316 CAKE (21,752/day).

- Official Oct-2026 mint breakdown: Farms 185,121; other product usage (lottery etc.) 123,953; Ecosystem Growth 365,242 ([Oct burn report](https://blog.pancakeswap.finance/articles/october-cake-burn-report)).

- Upcoming change: "The Flip" Step 1 cuts emissions to 11,000/day during a roughly 3-month chain-by-chain rollout starting Nov 2026. Step 2 cuts them to 7,000/day, all to "the Pantry" ecosystem fund, about 12 months later, when supply hits the −20% target. As of 2026-11-10 the BSC MasterChef v2 rate still implies ≈21.7k/day, so the emission cut was not yet live on-chain at read time.

