| 0x73feaa1eE314F8c655E354234017bE2193C9E24E (MasterChef v1) | 7,257,441 | 2.2% | Legacy staking contract |

| 0x5692DB8177a81A6c6afc8084C2976C9933EC1bAB (veCAKE) | 5,153,583 | 1.6% | Un-redeemed veCAKE after its 2025 retirement (1:1 redemption still being used: balance fell from 5,154,421 earlier the same day) |

| 0xA38E0dDBF8307C5949bf795Ba7F3F710Af956c82 | 3,010,423 | 0.9% | Unidentified EOA. Cast 3,010,423 of the 3,037,344 "For" votes on The Flip. |

Treasury: PancakeSwap does not publish a treasury address list in its docs. The Jan-2026 proposal said the Ecosystem Growth Fund held ~3.5M CAKE. A full treasury breakdown is not available.

### How it works

#### The product

- Spot AMM, three generations. v2 is constant-product with a 0.25% fee. v3 is concentrated liquidity with fee tiers of 0.01%/0.05%/0.25%/1%; LP positions are NFTs. Infinity (formerly v4, live on BNB Chain since Apr 2025) uses a singleton pool manager with "hooks" (dynamic fees, limit orders, Shared Inventory Hook for RWA/stock pools) and CLAMM plus Liquidity-Book pool types. There is also StableSwap (Curve-style) for pegged pairs.

- Execution layer. The Smart Router splits trades across v2/v3/StableSwap/Infinity and market-maker RFQ. PancakeSwap X is an intent/RFQ engine with gasless swaps and MEV protection. The Aggregator and "Unified Swap API" are open to third parties; the Aggregator routed more than $1B in a 30-day window in Oct 2026. MEV Guard RPC is also available.

- Side products: Prediction (5-minute BNB/BTC/ETH up/down rounds with a 3% fee), Lottery (CAKE tickets), CAKE.PAD (token sales paid in CAKE), Syrup Pools (stake CAKE, earn partner tokens), Dual Investment (launched Oct 2026), Perpetuals (simple/pro modes), the "Stock Terminal" for tokenized stocks/ETFs (Ondo, xStocks, Binance bStocks, Reality rTokens) and a "Pre-Access Portal" for tokenized pre-IPO exposure via Binance Wallet. Since a June-2026 vote, side-product fees go to Treasury rather than burn; the proposal put side products at "less than 2% of total protocol fees".

- Chains (11): BNB Chain, Ethereum, Arbitrum, Base, Solana, Robinhood Chain, Monad, Arc, zkSync Era, Linea, opBNB. Aptos also has a CAKE OFT and a deployment.

#### Fee split per swap (current, before The Flip completes)

| Pool | LP | CAKE buyback-and-burn | Treasury |

| --- | --- | --- | --- |

| v2 (0.25%) | 68% (0.17%) | 23% (0.0575%) | 9% (0.0225%) |

| v3 0.01% | 67% | 15% | 18% |

| v3 0.05% | 66% | 15% | 19% |

| v3 0.25% / 1% | 68% | 23% | 9% |

| v3 Solana (all tiers) | 84% | 8% | 8% |

| Infinity | ~67% | ~half of protocol share (DefiLlama methodology: 50/50 protocol/burn) | ~half of protocol share |

| Infinity on Robinhood Chain (since Sep 2026) | 90% | 10% protocol |  |

| StableSwap | 50% | 40% | 10% |

Sources: [docs: Trading fees](https://docs.pancakeswap.finance/earn/pancakeswap-pools.md), The Flip proposal table, DefiLlama adapter methodology. Since the Feb-2026 vote, Treasury-bound fees from USDT/USDC/USD1/U pools are kept in stablecoins instead of being converted to CAKE (≈29% of Treasury revenue by the team's estimate).

#### Token mechanics

- Buyback-and-burn: the protocol's burn share is used to buy CAKE on the open market. CAKE is accumulated and sent to 0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dEaD in a weekly batch (normally Mondays) by the burn admin 0xCEBA60280fb0ecd9A5A26A1552B90944770a4a0e, a 3-of-7 Gnosis Safe (on-chain getThreshold() = 3, 7 owners). The same Safe also burns the 99.7% emission discard from MasterChef v2, which is why individual burn transactions show 58–64M CAKE.

- Emissions: Kitchen-managed allocations to farms (v2/v3/Infinity), lottery and the Ecosystem Growth fund. Gauge voting was removed in Apr 2025.

- veCAKE / staking / revenue share: retired. Tokenomics 3.0 (vote 2025-04-15→18, 21.56M For / 0.24M Against) unlocked all veCAKE 1:1, ended revenue sharing (its 5% of 0.01%/0.05% pool fees went to burn), ended bribes and boosting, and cut emissions from ~40,000 to ~22,500/day.

- Governance: Snapshot space cakevote.eth, voted at pancakeswap.finance/voting. Proposals come from the Kitchen, and turnout is small (8 to 300 voters on recent votes). Snapshot results are not binding on-chain. Execution is by multisig: the MasterChef v2 owner is a Timelock (0xa1f482dc58145ba2210bc21878ca34000e2e8fe4, delay() = 21,700 s ≈ 6.0 h) whose admin is a 3-of-7 Gnosis Safe (0xecc90d54b10add1ab746abe7e83abe178b72aa9e; getThreshold() = 3, getOwners() = 7). Its 7 owners are the same 7 addresses as the burn Safe 0xceba…4a0e, so one signer set controls both emissions configuration and burns. Owner 0xd09971d8ed6c6a5e57581e90d593ee5b94e348d4 submitted every Safe burn transaction checked here.

- Not present: no fee switch to holders, no staking yield in CAKE, no gas use, no collateral role required by the protocol.

### Utility

What CAKE is actually needed for:

- Governance votes (Snapshot, balance-weighted; no lock needed since 2025).

- Committing to CAKE.PAD token sales. Committed CAKE is used and 100% of CAKE.PAD fees are burned; 2025 sales burned 51,262 / 67,027 / 39,683 CAKE ([2025 recap](https://blog.pancakeswap.finance/articles/2025-recap)).

- Buying Lottery tickets (20% of CAKE played is burned).

- Staking in Syrup Pools to earn partner tokens. This is partner-funded, not protocol yield.

- Farm rewards are paid in CAKE. CAKE is the incentive currency LPs receive and often sell.

What CAKE is NOT needed for: swapping, LPing, paying fees, perps margin, prediction bets (BNB), or Stock Terminal/Pre-Access trades. A trader never has to touch CAKE. Since Tokenomics 3.0 there is no cash-flow claim of any kind. In practice CAKE is a governance token with a revenue-funded buyback-and-burn plus a few participation utilities.

### Why people buy and sell it

Demand drivers

- Protocol buybacks: recurring, mechanical demand. The last 52 complete burn weeks saw 33.27M CAKE (≈$59.1M at burn-time prices) bought and burned, according to the burn dashboard. Recent weeks are much smaller at ≈$0.6–0.7M/week.

- Deflation narrative: "ultrasound CAKE", with 38 straight months of net supply reduction and the −20% by 2030 target.

- BNB Chain beta and Binance-ecosystem exposure: PancakeSwap is the default venue behind Binance Wallet / Binance Alpha flows and Binance TGEs (43 TGEs in 2025), and the #1 venue for Binance bStocks per the Kitchen. CAKE trades as a high-beta proxy for BNB Chain on-chain activity.

- Narratives: tokenized stocks/RWA (Stock Terminal, Pre-Access Portal), Infinity hooks, expansion to Robinhood Chain and Circle's Arc.

- Participation demand for CAKE.PAD sales (oversubscribed 678x to 1,425x in 2025).

Supply / sell pressure

- ≈21.7k CAKE/day of emissions (≈$39k/day at $1.81). Much of it goes to farmers who sell.

- The Ecosystem Growth fund and the future "Pantry" (7k CAKE/day), which the Kitchen can deploy "flexibly" on marketing and partnerships.

- Treasury sales for USD opex. The Feb-2026 proposal says Treasury sold CAKE to pay "Chefs' salaries"; stablecoin retention reduces this.

- About 35% of supply sits in two addresses believed to be Binance custody wallets. These hold customer balances, not a seller, but they concentrate exchange liquidity.

- No VC/team unlock overhang.

