### Key people

- Structure: anonymous core team called "the Kitchen". Contributors are pseudonymous "Chefs": 37 are listed on the team page (checked 2026-11-10). No foundation, company or legal entity is disclosed in the docs. Media have long reported a close Binance association, but there is no official confirmation of ownership. Binance Wallet/Alpha, bStocks and Binance Blockchain Week are deep operational partners. Governance proposals are authored by the Kitchen, and on-chain control sits with two 3-of-7 Gnosis Safes that share the same 7 owners, plus a ~6-hour Timelock (Section 3).

- Chef Kids — Head Chef (X: [@Headchef_pcs](https://x.com/Headchef_pcs)). Spoke at KBW2026 Seoul on 2026-09-30 per the Sep Kitchen Report.

- Chef Mochi — the earlier public Head Chef (Token Terminal interview, 2023). Not on the current team page; no dated handover announcement found, so treat as a departure from the head role.

- Other listed leads ([The Kitchen Team](https://docs.pancakeswap.finance/welcome-to-pancakeswap/about-us/team/the-kitchen-team.md)): Chef Miso and Chef Kocha (Product); Chef Mustard (Ops, [@chef_mustard](https://twitter.com/chef_mustard)); Chef Leo (BD Lead, [@DYOR_WAGMI](https://x.com/DYOR_WAGMI)); Chef Cocoa (Marketing Lead, [@chef_cocoa_pcs](https://x.com/chef_cocoa_pcs)); Chef Alina (Partnership Marketing, [@0xalinatyng](https://x.com/0xalinatyng)); Chef Mist (Dev Lead); Chef Snoopy (Smart Contract Dev Lead); Chef Taco (Backend Lead); Chef Ryan (Frontend Lead); Chef Rei (Security); Chef Cyrus (Data). Open roles listed in the docs: Business Development Lead, Senior Designer, Business Development Manager (Liquidity Hub), Quant Developer, Head of Marketing.

- Official accounts: [@PancakeSwap](https://x.com/PancakeSwap); forum forum.pancakeswap.finance; blog blog.pancakeswap.finance.

### Recent news (last ~90 days)

- 2026-11-09 — The weekly CAKE buyback-and-burn was postponed one week to 2026-11-16 for audits and security upgrades of the buyback contracts "following recent industry incidents". The team says user funds and trading are unaffected ([Crypto Economy](https://crypto-economy.com/pancakeswap-postpones-cake-buyback-amid-security-upgrades/), [The Crypto Times](https://www.cryptotimes.io/2026/11/09/pancakeswap-delays-cake-buyback-and-burn-amid-security-review/)). Crypto Economy quotes the @PancakeSwap X post of 2026-11-09 ("Because this work touches the contracts that handle trading fee buybacks, this week's trading fee…"). Consistent with this, the burn dashboard shows only lottery burns (28,305 CAKE) for the 2026-11-09 week.

- 2026-11-06/07 (secondary, unverified) — Binance began phased resumption of CAKE (and other assets) withdrawals as part of a "ninth recovery update following a security incident"; deposits stayed open ([CoinMarketCap AI summary citing TokenPost](https://coinmarketcap.com/cmc-ai/pancakeswap/latest-updates/)). This exchange-side incident was not confirmed from a Binance primary source in this review and is relevant because ≈35% of CAKE supply sits in two Binance-labelled wallets.

- by 2026-11-07 — The Flip's first switch went live on Robinhood Chain: v3 and Infinity LPs there get 88% of swap fees ([Coinfomania, 2026-11-07](https://coinfomania.com/robinhood-chain-launches-the-flip-with-pancakeswap/), citing PancakeSwap's X announcement; CoinMarketCap's AI summary dates it 2026-11-08). The primary X post was not retrieved.

- 2026-11-04 — October burn report: 38th straight month of net reduction, −1,116,211 CAKE.

- Early Nov 2026 (unverified) — Reports of DeFi security incidents in late October, which PancakeSwap cited as the reason for its buyback-contract upgrade. An earlier draft also said PancakeSwap took its GitBook-hosted docs offline after a 2026-11-02 GitBook breach; no source for that could be retrieved, and docs.pancakeswap.finance was serving pages on 2026-11-10.

- 2026-10-24 — The Flip passed: 3,037,344 For vs 1,245,165 Against, 43 voters. As of 2026-10-22 it was losing 97.8% Against (999,487 vs 22,202; one wallet 0x3DDd…e1ad cast 765,559 Against). On 2026-10-23 07:22 UTC wallet 0xA38E…6c82 cast 3,010,423 For, 99.1% of all For votes ([AltcoinBuzz](https://www.altcoinbuzz.io/pancakeswap-s-the-flip-faces-98-opposition-ahead-of-vote-close); Snapshot API).

- Oct 2026 — Dual Investment launched on BNB Chain (BTC/BNB/ETH). Infinity passed $150B cumulative volume. The Aggregator passed $1B routed in 30 days. KuCoin Web3 Wallet integrated PancakeSwap X. The Shared Inventory Hook began powering four.meme "stock memes". PancakeSwap became the trading layer for De1's Tokenized Asset World.

- 2026-10-14 — The Flip discussion published ([Crypto Briefing](https://cryptobriefing.com/pancakeswap-88-lp-fee-share-cake-emissions/); [forum](https://forum.pancakeswap.finance/t/proposal-discussion-the-flip-liquidity-should-get-paid-more/1658)).

- 2026-09-29 — Infinity went live on Circle's Arc L1.

- Sep 2026 — Robinhood Chain: all Infinity pools moved to 90% LP / 10% protocol ([Kitchen Report Sep 2026](https://blog.pancakeswap.finance/articles/kitchen-report-september-2026); the exact date is not stated there).

- Sep 2026 — Pre-Access Portal launched. The first deal, $pPOLY (Paimon Finance), filled a $50M cap in 1 min 36 s, 10× oversubscribed, with 9,091 participants. The Stock Terminal added Ondo portfolios, Reality rTokens and SHEINx. PancakeSwap became the #1 venue for Binance bStocks (~$75M in a 24h snapshot). Launchpads pair.fun and genius.fun began graduating into Infinity. A 6th anniversary was celebrated 2026-09-22. September net burn was −0.70%, and CAKE peaked at about $2.83.

- Aug 2026 — Kitchen Report Aug 2026 and August burn report. Volume rebounded to $26.2B (DefiLlama) after a July low of $18.5B.

### Current problems and risks

- Shrinking business. Monthly volume is −78% YoY (Oct 2025 $110.2B → Oct 2026 $24.3B), fees −85% ($78.3M → $11.8M) and holder revenue −85% ($17.2M → $2.6M). TVL is −18% YoY. Weekly burns in USD fell from $2.03M (2026-09-14 week) to $0.59–0.72M in late Oct to early Nov.

- Thinning deflation margin. Net deflation now rests on about 290–360k CAKE burned per week against 152k emitted. Another volume drop, or the BSC v3 switch under The Flip, could push it toward neutral. Lower emissions (11k, then 7k/day) offset this.

- Value capture weakened by design. The Flip sends v3/Infinity protocol fees to the Treasury rather than to the burn. Side-product fees were already redirected in June 2026, and stablecoin fees are retained since Feb 2026. Each step moves value from holders toward the Kitchen-controlled Treasury.

- Governance centralization. Votes are decided by 1–2 wallets. The Flip turned from 98% Against to passing on a single 3.01M-CAKE wallet whose identity is unknown. The team is anonymous, and execution is by two 3-of-7 multisigs with the same 7 owners and only a ~6-hour timelock.

- Dependency on Binance / BNB Chain. About 94% of fees come from BSC, flows depend on Binance Wallet/Alpha, and roughly 35% of supply sits in two wallets believed to be Binance custody (one label unverified). A change in Binance's routing or incentives (as with Alpha points) moves PancakeSwap volume directly.

- Security and operations. The buyback was postponed for contract security upgrades (Nov 2026), with no reported loss of funds. Binance reportedly had its own security incident and resumed CAKE withdrawals in phases from 2026-11-06 (secondary source only). Multichain sprawl (11 chains, opBNB bridge sunset) adds surface area.

- Competition. Uniswap leads total volume (2.6× PancakeSwap's 30d volume) and is the #2 venue on BSC (8.8%). On Solana and Base, PancakeSwap is minor (Solana v3 TVL $6.2M, Base $18.9M).

- Data reliability. Official volume claims (2025: $2.36T) far exceed DefiLlama's ($670B), so headline "#1 DEX" claims should not be taken at face value.

What the market still believes in: CAKE as one of the few large DeFi tokens with a real, recurring, revenue-funded buyback and multi-year net deflation (38 months); PancakeSwap as Binance's on-chain distribution layer for TGEs, tokenized stocks and pre-IPO products; and Infinity hooks as a product moat.

