As of 2026-11-10

### Executive summary

AERO is the single token of Aero (the merged successor of Aerodrome Finance on Base and Velodrome on OP Mainnet), the cross-chain spot DEX that went live on 2026-10-22 00:00 UTC as the merger of Aerodrome (Base) and Velodrome (OP Mainnet), both built by Dromos Labs. The new AERO is an ERC-20 on Base (0x3f5bF3EdAc59d650D8fDf9657a71F2f904A3a4Ee). It replaced old AERO 1:1 and VELO at 0.044 AERO per VELO. Value does reach holders today, but only holders who stake as sAERO and allocate rewards to pools. They receive 100% of pool-level "exchange revenue" (swap fees from AERO-earning liquidity, the unstaked-fee cut, and Liquidity/Launch Payments, i.e. bribes) in real time. That was about $1.85M in the last 7 days per DefiLlama and about $4.7M over the first 20 days after launch, roughly $85M annualized. Against this, AERO is diluted by about 9.6% a year: on-chain, 11.09M AERO were minted in the first 19.66 days, and the dollar value of AERO rewards currently runs above exchange revenue. The state is mixed. The merger launched cleanly with no reported exploit, and Aero holds 53% of Base DEX volume. But protocol revenue is down roughly 80–85% from its Q4 2024 peak, the token is about 31% below its 2026-10-23 post-launch high ($0.5426 vs $0.7845, CoinGecko), and the migration is unfinished (about 373M new AERO still sit unclaimed in the migration contracts on 2026-11-10 15:56 UTC). The single most important thing to watch is whether weekly exchange revenue grows faster than AERO issuance, now about 3.9M AERO a week. In practice that means the ratio of the Aero dashboard's weekly revenue to the weekly emission value, plus whether Momentum Fund buyback/burn activity starts.

### What the token is

#### Identity and contracts

- Ticker: AERO (token name on-chain: "Aero"). CoinGecko id aero. The legacy token remains listed as aerodrome-finance, and most CEX tickers (Coinbase, Binance, Kraken, Bybit, Upbit, Bithumb) are still mapped there on CoinGecko as of 2026-11-10.

- Chain: AERO exists only on Base. On Ethereum, OP Mainnet, Arbitrum, Ink, Robinhood Chain, Arc and Elysium, rewards are paid in xAERO, a per-chain receipt token redeemable 1:1 for AERO on Base. It is burned on the leaf chain and minted on Base, and is not cross-chain transferable between leaf chains ([Aero docs: AERO and sAERO](https://app.aero.xyz/docs/about/aero-and-saero)).

- New AERO token (Base): 0x3f5bF3EdAc59d650D8fDf9657a71F2f904A3a4Ee. Verified against the official [Aero docs security page](https://app.aero.xyz/docs/security/), and on-chain name() = "Aero". It reads MINTER() = 0x59268A34ba897e82368feE39839FFC661D4f9C97 (Minter), VOTING_ESCROW() = 0xBF7977E1521e9a3032bf7243Ee4712f311f13915 (sAERO), MIGRATION() = 0x22a2F7340a3fB4C7C389D91eE954766B12476721 (AerodromeMigration) and VELODROME_MIGRATION() = 0x6daE95FE833f190640dB1176F8C8a2e50C6a66c0 (VelodromeMigrationEntrypoint on Base; the same address is the VelodromeMigration contract on OP Mainnet per the security page).

- sAERO (staking NFT / VotingEscrow, Base): 0xBF7977E1521e9a3032bf7243Ee4712f311f13915.

- Legacy tokens: old AERO 0x940181a94A35A4569E4529A3CDfB74e38FD98631 (Base), old veAERO 0xeBf418Fe2512e7E6bd9b87a8F0f294aCDC67e6B4, VELO 0x9560e827aF36c94D2Ac33a39bCE1Fe78631088Db (OP Mainnet). Upgrading is one-way and has no deadline ([Aero Upgrade Hub](https://aero.xyz/aero-upgrade/)).

#### Supply (on-chain reads, Base block 55,679,160, 2026-11-10 ~15:56 UTC; re-read by the fact-checker)

