| New AERO totalSupply | 2,138,235,494 AERO (2,138,185,755 at block 55,654,893, ~14:35 UTC) | totalSupply() on 0x3f5b…a4Ee |

| Staked as sAERO (VotingEscrow supply()) | 1,063,412,889 AERO (49.7%) | VotingEscrow 0xBF79…3915 |

| …of which Perpetual (permanent) stakes | 950,459,336 AERO (89.4% of staked) | permanentStakeBalance() |

| sAERO positions minted (NFT id counter) | 23,937 | tokenId() |

| Unclaimed in Aerodrome migration contract | 347,140,279 AERO | remaining() on 0x22a2…6721 (equals its AERO balanceOf); paidBasis() = 1,662,859,721 already paid out |

| Unclaimed in Velodrome migration entrypoint (Base) | 25,818,486 AERO (of ~117M Velodrome allocation; 27,597,235 at ~14:35 UTC) | balanceOf 0x6daE…66c0 |

| Residual "liquid, outside staking and migration" | ~701.9M AERO (computed) | 2,138.24 − 1,063.41 − 347.14 − 25.82 (millions) |

| CoinGecko circulating / total / max | 699,200,614 / 2,135,578,125 / none | [CoinGecko API](https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/coins/aero), last_updated 2026-11-10 15:55 UTC. CoinGecko's "circulating" excludes sAERO, which is non-standard. |

| Aero dashboard | Total 2.14B; staked 1.06B (49.64%); avg stake duration 3.93 years | [aero.xyz/economics/metrics](https://aero.xyz/economics/metrics/), pulled 2026-11-10T07:17Z |

Conversion progress (computed from the reads above): about 82.7% of the Aerodrome-side 2.01B allocation and about 78% of the Velodrome-side ~117M allocation had been claimed by 2026-11-10 15:56 UTC. On the legacy side, old AERO totalSupply is unchanged at 2,007,626,316. Upgraded liquid old AERO is routed by the migration contract into the old veAERO contract, which now holds 1,712,968,050 old AERO. The rest, ~294.7M old AERO, is still outside it, including CEX balances. On OP Mainnet, the old veVELO contract (0xFAf8FD17D9840595845582fCB047DF13f006787d) holds 2,193,397,914 of 2,659,623,321 VELO (OP RPC read, 2026-11-10).

#### Issuance / emissions

- No fixed schedule. AERO Rewards stream per second to pools, as directed by sAERO allocation. They are capped per pool by "Gauge Caps" set at a multiple of projected pool revenue (target ~1.2x over time; the docs give 1.1–1.4x as healthy). AERO above a cap, or forfeited by LPs who exit before "MinStake time", is never minted. Tokens are minted only when LPs claim ([docs: Emissions](https://app.aero.xyz/docs/about/emissions), [docs: Gauges](https://app.aero.xyz/docs/features/gauges)).

- Hard ceiling: 20% annualized at launch. On-chain, the Minter's baseRate() = 13.489345 AERO/second, about 425M AERO/yr, about 19.9% of current supply. The project's "expected realized" rate is ~12% ([Upgrade Hub](https://aero.xyz/aero-upgrade/)), and its Oct 19 article says about 8% at 1.2x rewards and then-current valuation ([The Aero Economy](https://aero.xyz/articles/the-aero-economy/)).

- Realized so far (on-chain): Minter emissionsMinted() = 11,088,883 AERO between ACTIVATION_TIMESTAMP 2026-10-22 00:00 UTC and 2026-11-10 15:56 UTC (19.66 days). That is ~564k AERO/day, ~206M/yr, ~9.6% of supply annualized (estimate, linear extrapolation). emissionsCap() read 22,918,505, which equals baseRate() × seconds since activation, i.e. the cumulative ceiling accrued to date, so actual minting is about 48% of the ceiling.

- Aero dashboard, week of 2026-11-05: 3.91M AERO emitted, of which 3.73M to LPs, 0 rebase and 171.59K team.

- Team/contributor share: 5% of emissions. For every 100 AERO claimed by LPs, 5 are minted to the Aero Foundation and held as a Perpetual Stake, and this is capped at the contract level (docs). On-chain, Minter teamRate() = 50000 (5%), the same as MAXIMUM_TEAM_RATE(). The Splitter (0x9Beb95cc…1156) lists two recipients (0xc59b7390…ea5f, 0x834c0da0…da52), each at 50% weight. Their off-chain identities are not labelled on-chain.

- No VC/insider unlock schedule. The new supply was 100% allocated to existing AERO/veAERO/VELO/veVELO holders (94.5% Aerodrome side = 2.01B, 5.5% Velodrome side = 117M), with no token sale or new team allocation ([launch post](https://aero.xyz/articles/aero-launches-today/)). The main forward supply flows are (1) emissions, (2) the ~373.0M AERO still to be claimed via migration (2026-11-10 15:56 UTC), which become liquid or staked when holders upgrade, and (3) sAERO expiries: decaying stakes can only be withdrawn at expiry and there is no early exit.

#### Large holders / treasury

- The largest single balances are protocol contracts: sAERO VotingEscrow (1.06B), the Aerodrome migration contract (347.1M) and the Velodrome entrypoint (25.8M) (2026-11-10 15:56 UTC).

- The Momentum Fund, run by the Aero Foundation, holds "one of the largest sAERO positions" (exact size not published in the documents reviewed). Aero's dashboard, lifetime through 2026-11-10, reports 180.39M AERO "bought back or locked" across programs: Claimed Voting 41.01M, Momentum Fund 110.40M (series includes predecessor Aerodrome programs), Project Relays 6.37M, veAERO Maxi 22.61M ([metrics](https://aero.xyz/economics/metrics/)).

- Coinbase Ventures / the Base Ecosystem Fund bought AERO on the open market from February 2024 and used veAERO votes to seed cbBTC pools ([CoinDesk 2024-02-27](https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2024/02/27/aero-surges-77-after-cb-ventures-invests-in-aerodrome-finance/); [Aero Economy](https://aero.xyz/articles/the-aero-economy/)). Its current sAERO size is not published.

### How it works

#### The exchange

- Pools: "Slipstream" (V3) concentrated-liquidity pools, a Uniswap-V3-style AMM with tick spacings, dynamic fees and an optional MEV tax, plus "Basic" volatile/stable pools (Solidly-style x*y=k and stable curve). Pool and gauge creation is permissionless.

- Two LP modes:

- AERO-earning (staked) LPs stake their position in the pool's gauge and earn AERO Rewards. Only in-range ("active tick") liquidity earns. Their swap fees ("Smart Fees" = trading fee + dynamic-fee premium + MEV tax) go to sAERO holders.

- Fee-earning (unstaked) LPs keep their fees minus an "unstaked fee". At launch this is 0% on Ethereum, Arbitrum and Robinhood Chain, and 5% on Base, OP Mainnet, Ink and Arc ([Aero Economy](https://aero.xyz/articles/the-aero-economy/)). On-chain, the Base WETH/USDC CL50 pool reads unstakedFee() = 50000 (5%).

- Dynamic fees: per-pool fees rise in volatile periods via a swap-fee hook (DynamicSwapFeeHook 0xC0ed888A…e434). Example: the WETH/USDC CL50 pool on Base charged an average of 3.9 bps in calm periods and 8.3 bps in volatile ones (Sep 11–Oct 6, 2026, per Aero). On-chain fee() read 1475, 896 and 735 (millionths, i.e. 0.1475%, 0.0896% and 0.0735%) at different times on 2026-11-10 between ~14:35 and ~16:00 UTC.

- MEV tax: swaps whose priority fee exceeds a retail-typical threshold pay an extra fee to LPs or sAERO holders, on supported L2s.

- Metaswaps / MetaRouter: bridge, route and swap across Aero chains in one transaction using Aero's own liquidity, with cross-chain messaging via Hyperlane adapters. "Programmable fee rebates" for aggregators and desks are announced.

#### The token engine ("AER Engine" + Predictive Allocation)

- Stake AERO into sAERO (an NFT) for any period up to 4 years, or as a "Perpetual Stake". Allocation Power = amount × time remaining / 4 years, decaying linearly, while perpetual stakes keep maximum weight. There is no early exit from a decaying stake, and stakes can be extended but not shortened. Existing veAERO/veVELO converted with their remaining lock time, rounded up to the next week, and permanent locks became max-duration sAERO. sAERO positions are transferable and tradable NFTs.

- Allocate ("Predictive Allocation"): sAERO holders point Allocation Power at pools on any Aero chain in one Base transaction. AERO Rewards then stream to those pools continuously. There are no weekly epochs, votes or rebases, and each stake has a 47-hour cooldown between reallocations. In return the holder earns a pro-rata share of that pool's revenue while the allocation is live.

- Gauge caps: cap = (projected trading fees + MEV tax + scheduled 48h incentives) × policy multiplier, converted to a dollar budget of AERO. Rewards are set in dollars, so a higher AERO price means fewer tokens minted. Caps are set by a protocol-governance multisig (CAP_ADMIN_ROLE) and an operator multisig (CAP_OPERATOR_ROLE) within a range ([security page](https://app.aero.xyz/docs/security/)).

- Autopilot (reported live around 2026-11-01; launch date not confirmed from a primary source): a managed vault that allocates for sAERO holders and either compounds revenue into sAERO or converts it to a target token such as USDC. It can charge a configurable performance fee ([docs](https://app.aero.xyz/docs/features/autopilot)).

- Incentives ("Liquidity Payments" / "Launch Payments"), historically called bribes: token issuers stream tokens per second to the sAERO holders allocating to their pool, to attract AERO Rewards.

- Momentum Fund (Aero Foundation): an sAERO position whose revenue can be held in reserve, used for "market-aware" buybacks and burns of AERO or sAERO, or paid to contributors ("Align"). Unlike the old fixed rebase, burns are discretionary.

- Governance: there is no token-vote proposal system in the Ve(3,3) sense. "Governance" means sAERO allocation, plus parameter administration by the Foundation and multisigs. An Emergency Council multisig can deactivate or reactivate gauges (set caps to zero), pause migration contracts and replace itself. Access-control roles (GOVERNANCE_ROLE, SPLITTER_CONFIG_ROLE, CHAIN_STATUS_ROLE, SEIZER_ROLE and others) are listed on the security page. Core contracts are described as immutable.

- Security: three ChainSecurity code audits plus a design review, two Sherlock audits, a three-week Sherlock public contest (Aug–Sep 2026, $400k pot announced) and an additional "Mythos-powered" review. Sherlock bug bounty up to $500,000 ([security page](https://app.aero.xyz/docs/security/); [Jul 16 update](https://aero.xyz/articles/aero-is-on-the-horizon/)).

#### For a regular user

A trader swaps on app.aero.xyz or via an aggregator such as Matcha or the Base app routing, and pays a dynamic pool fee. An LP deposits into a pool and chooses either to earn fees (minus 0–5%) or to stake for AERO rewards. A token holder stakes AERO, picks pools (or uses Autopilot), and receives a stream of mixed tokens: swap fees in pool tokens plus incentive tokens. Gas for allocation is paid on Base only.

### Utility

- Real utility:

- (1) Staked AERO (sAERO) is the only way to direct AERO emissions, and the only claim on exchange revenue. 100% of pool-level revenue goes to sAERO allocators.

- (2) AERO is the currency LPs are paid in.

- (3) Issuers and ecosystems that want liquidity either buy and stake AERO to allocate to their own pools, as Coinbase Ventures and the Foundation did for cbBTC, or pay Liquidity Payments to sAERO holders. This creates real demand for sAERO.

- Not needed for: trading on Aero (fees are paid in pool tokens, not AERO), gas (ETH on all chains), or being an LP (fee-earning LPs never touch AERO). Liquid, unstaked AERO earns nothing and has no governance weight. All economic rights sit in sAERO.

- Governance-only? No. sAERO carries a cash-flow claim, but it is conditional on active allocation, or on delegating to Autopilot. Protocol parameters such as fee rates, caps, chain additions and the team-share recipient are controlled by the Foundation and multisigs, not by token votes.

### Why people buy and sell it

#### Demand drivers

- Cash-flow yield: about $85M/yr annualized holder revenue since launch (estimate, DefiLlama) on 1.06B sAERO is roughly $0.08 per sAERO per year, about 14–15% nominal at $0.55. Before dilution, emissions run at ~9.6%/yr, mostly paid to LPs, not to stakers.

- Bribe-market demand: issuers such as tokenized-stock pools, Base ecosystem tokens and new chains (Arc, Robinhood Chain, Elysium) pay sAERO holders. In Sept 2026, $8.9M of $14.9M revenue was Liquidity/Launch Payments ([Aero Economy](https://aero.xyz/articles/the-aero-economy/)).

- Narratives:

- "Base's liquidity hub" and the Coinbase alignment, including Coinbase Ventures' holdings and Coinbase Tokenized Stocks launching with day-one liquidity on Aerodrome on 2026-08-24.

- Tokenized equities: Aero says its share of Ethereum+L2 tokenized-stock DEX trading went from single digits in August to over 50% on 2026-10-10.

- Onchain FX (EURC), where Aero claims more FX volume than every other DEX combined in H1 2026.

- BTC-dollar trading, where Aero claims the top DEX in Q3 2026.

- A multi-chain expansion that Aero says gives it access to ~4x the DEX volume of Base+OP, and a "no VC, 100% revenue to stakers" story.

- Base token speculation: Base said in September 2025 it was "beginning to explore" a network token ([The Block](https://www.theblock.co/post/370668/coinbase-incubated-base-network-beginning-to-explore-native-token-creator-jesse-pollak-says)). No launch has been announced as of 2026-11-10. Aero is a common proxy trade for Base.

- Listings and derivatives: AERO trades on Coinbase, Binance (spot and USDⓈ-M perp), Kraken, Bybit, Upbit, Bithumb, KuCoin, Gate, Bitget and others (CoinGecko tickers for the legacy id). Perp open interest on 2026-11-10 ~15:58 UTC: Binance 46.20M AERO (~$25.3M at $0.5466 mark), Bybit 22.71M AERO (~$12.4M). Funding was slightly positive (Binance last rate 0.0021% per 4h interval; Bybit 0.005% per 4h) ([Binance premiumIndex](https://fapi.binance.com/fapi/v1/premiumIndex?symbol=AEROUSDT), [fundingInfo](https://fapi.binance.com/fapi/v1/fundingInfo)).

#### Supply and sell pressure

- Emissions: ~3.9M AERO a week (~$2.2M/week at $0.55) paid to LPs. Many LPs are mercenary and sell rewards, so this is the main structural sell flow. In the Sept 2026 example, AERO paid to LPs ($10.5M in 4 weeks) was below revenue ($14.9M). In the latest week, the value of the 3.73M AERO to LPs (~$2.05M) is above Aero's own weekly revenue figure ($1.3M) and slightly above DefiLlama's 7d holder revenue ($1.85M).

- Migration overhang: ~373.0M AERO are still claimable (2026-11-10 15:56 UTC). Part of that is already-liquid exchange inventory being re-papered, which is not new selling, but it does add to tradable supply when claimed.

- Merger-related selling: both AERO and VELO fell ~20% the day the merger was announced (2025-11-13; [FXStreet](https://www.fxstreet.com/cryptocurrencies/news/aerodrome-velodrome-tokens-plunge-20-following-merger-unveil-202511131826)). New AERO peaked at $0.7845 on 2026-10-23 and was $0.5426 (−31%) on 2026-11-10 15:55 UTC (CoinGecko).

- No VC/team unlock cliffs. The 5% team emission share accrues to a Foundation Perpetual Stake, so it is not designed to be liquid.

### The protocol/business

- What it is: a spot DEX and liquidity marketplace, "the unified liquidity layer for all of Ethereum". It runs on MetaDEX03, Dromos Labs' third-generation ve(3,3)-derived design. Lineage: Velodrome launched on Optimism in 2022, and Aerodrome launched on Base in August 2023 with 500M initial AERO, 450M of it as veAERO. Final pre-merger supplies were 2.0026B AERO and 2.6485B VELO ([docs](https://app.aero.xyz/docs/about/emissions)).

- Chains (8 live): Base (root), Ethereum, OP Mainnet, Arbitrum, Ink, Robinhood Chain and Arc at launch on 2026-10-22, plus Elysium (Kinetiq's Hyperliquid L2), which appears in Aero's contract list and in DefiLlama fee data from 2026-11-09. Velodrome continues on Celo, Fraxtal, Soneium and Unichain without a token economy.

- Product lines: swaps (direct, aggregators, Metaswaps); LP pools (Slipstream V3, Basic); sAERO staking and allocation, plus Autopilot; incentive and launch programs for issuers; "Aero Lite", a lightweight deployment for new chains (live on Arc since 2026-09-16); the Sugar SDK and on-chain data contracts for agents and integrators. Planned: an sAERO marketplace, Metaswap fees and other "Service Revenue" (the "REV Engine").

- Audience: Base retail (via the Coinbase/Base app and aggregators), professional market makers and arbitrageurs, token issuers bootstrapping liquidity (Base memecoins, AI tokens such as VVV, Coinbase Tokenized Stocks, cbBTC, EURC), and chains seeking day-one liquidity (Arc, Robinhood Chain, Ink, Elysium). Most activity is on Base, which is US- and Coinbase-centric. Coinbase Tokenized Stocks are for eligible non-US jurisdictions. Korean exchanges (Upbit, Bithumb, Coinone) list AERO.

- Top pools (on-chain, Base): WETH/USDC CL50 0x4a7af46b…366c: pool balances 3,561 WETH + 1.31M USDC, 96.0% of in-range liquidity staked; 24h on-chain volume $7.70M from 2,433 Swap events (2026-11-09/10). Others: cbBTC/USDC CL50/CL100, cbBTC/WETH CL1, WETH/USDT, EURC/USDC, and Coinbase tokenized-stock pools (SNDKc, MSTRc, METAc, SPCXc, AMZNc, NVDAc, GOOGLc, TSLAc, MSFTc paired with USDC). The new Base CL factory had 608 pools on 2026-11-10.

