### Revenue and value capture

#### Mechanism (exact flow)

- Swap fees from staked (AERO-earning) liquidity accrue inside the pool (gaugeFees()). They are swept by the gauge via the pool's collectFees(), which emits CollectFees(recipient, amount0, amount1), into the pool's rewards contract. On Base WETH/USDC CL50 the recipient is 0x623de2a4cb208e8498ae888ec1ec805a105fef48. sAERO holders allocated to that pool then claim pro-rata. Verified on-chain: in the last 24h, this contract received 1,842.09 USDC and 1.1946 WETH, exclusively from the pool.

- Unstaked fee (0–5% of fee-earning LP fees) is routed to the same sAERO allocators.

- Liquidity/Launch Payments (bribes): streamed per second to sAERO allocators via each pool's rewards contract (gauge→rewards mapping in FactoryRegistry.gaugeToRewards).

- No protocol treasury cut and no automatic buyback/burn. "100% of exchange revenue accrues to the token or its holders." Burns happen only through Momentum Fund discretion, or later through planned Service-Revenue fees (sAERO marketplace, Metaswap fee). The Foundation earns as an sAERO holder, plus the 5% emission share.

