Reconciliation. DefiLlama's 7d holder revenue ($1.85M) and Aero's latest weekly figure ($1.3M) differ by window (rolling 7d vs. the dashboard's week starting Nov 5, which may be partial) and by method. Both include Liquidity Payments. Our independent on-chain sample shows that swap fees are the minority of current revenue. Summing CollectFees events over 7 days (Base blocks ~55.35M–55.66M) for the 25 highest-volume Aero Slipstream pools on Base (by GeckoTerminal ranking) gives roughly $91.5k of swap fees routed to sAERO over 7 days, priced at DefiLlama current prices (estimate; 1 of ~775 log queries failed after retries). About 46% of that ($41.9k) came from 13 Coinbase tokenized-stock pools, and the largest single pool was WETH/USDC CL50 at $13.3k. DefiLlama's 7d Base holders revenue is $1.51M (Nov 3–9, the window behind total7d). The remainder must come from Liquidity/Launch Payments, long-tail and high-fee pools, Basic pools, and fees that DefiLlama measures via pendingFees growth. We could not decompose it further with public endpoints. Conclusion: real value reaches sAERO holders today, but it is mostly paid by issuers via bribes, not by traders. Organic swap-fee capture on blue-chip pools is small: WETH/USDC CL50 sends ~$4.3k/day to sAERO at ~5 bps effective on $7.7M daily volume.

Value vs. dilution (estimate): annualized holder revenue ~$85M vs. annualized emissions ~206M AERO (~$112M at $0.5426, CoinGecko 2026-11-10 15:55 UTC), of which ~95% goes to LPs. On a per-token basis: holder revenue / FDV (CoinGecko FDV $1.159B) ≈ 7.3%/yr, and holder revenue / sAERO value (1.063B × $0.5426 ≈ $577M) ≈ 14.7%/yr, before ~9.6% supply growth.

Monetization plan beyond today: raise unstaked fees as pools dominate; add Service Revenue (sAERO marketplace fees collected in sAERO and burned, Metaswap fees used for buyback/burn, builder products); Momentum Fund market-aware buybacks and burns; and the MEV tax and dynamic fees ([The Aero Economy](https://aero.xyz/articles/the-aero-economy/)). None of the Service Revenue lines had published launch dates as of 2026-11-10.

### How to verify on-chain

All calls below use the public Base RPC https://base-rpc.publicnode.com. Values are what the original researcher obtained on 2026-11-10 ~14:35–15:10 UTC (Base blocks ~55.65M–55.66M) and, after the arrow "FC", what the fact-checker re-read at ~15:56 UTC (block 55,679,160). Results are hex uint256 with 18 decimals for AERO. All commands below were re-run and work as written.

#### 1. Supply and staking

# AERO totalSupply -> 2,138,185,755 AERO ; FC 2,138,235,494curl -s -X POST https://base-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0x3f5bF3EdAc59d650D8fDf9657a71F2f904A3a4Ee","data":"0x18160ddd"},"latest"]}'# sAERO staked: VotingEscrow.supply() -> 1,061,625,750 AERO (15:10 UTC) ; FC 1,063,412,889curl -s -X POST https://base-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0xBF7977E1521e9a3032bf7243Ee4712f311f13915","data":"0x047fc9aa"},"latest"]}'# permanentStakeBalance() = 0xac35199d -> 948,677,404 (FC 950,459,336) ; totalVotingPower() = 0x671b3793 -> 1,042,082,177 (FC 1,043,926,674)# tokenId() = 0x17d70f7c -> sAERO NFTs minted (FC 23,937)

#### 2. Emissions

