- Structure:

- Dromos Labs ([dromos.xyz](https://dromos.xyz/)) is the core development company that built MetaDEX01–03, the Sugar SDK, Superswaps and VerifiedERC20. Per the docs it "does not own the protocol, control its governance, or hold a special claim on its revenue".

- The Aero Foundation (the docs also say "Aerodrome Foundation") is a non-profit steward. It administers parameters (fee rates, gauge-cap bounds, deployments), runs the Momentum Fund and receives the 5% emission share.

- Multisigs (protocol governance, operator, Emergency Council) hold privileged roles. sAERO holders steer emissions.

- Several team members are pseudonymous by policy. Official X accounts: [@aeroxyz](https://x.com/aeroxyz), plus legacy [@aerodromefi](https://x.com/aerodromefi) and [@VelodromeFi](https://x.com/VelodromeFi). GitHub: [Dromos-Labs](https://github.com/Dromos-Labs).

- Departures: none found in the reviewed sources. One November 2025 merger report quoted a "Luis de la Cerda" of Dromos, who is not on the current Dromos team page (not verified).

- Auditors: Riley Holterhus led the audit effort (Jul 16, 2026 update).

### Recent news (last ~90 days)

- 2026-08-24 — Coinbase Tokenized Stocks (B20 tokens on Base, backed 1:1 by shares) launch with day-one liquidity on Aerodrome ([Aero](https://aero.xyz/articles/coinbase-tokenized-stocks-launch-on-aerodrome/)).

- August–September 2026 — Sherlock public audit contest for Aero (three weeks, $400k pot announced in the Jul 16 update; the security page dates it "August to September 2026", exact start/end dates not published there) ([Jul 16 update](https://aero.xyz/articles/aero-is-on-the-horizon/); [security page](https://app.aero.xyz/docs/security/)). The launch had slipped from the original "Q2 2026" target ([The Defiant](https://thedefiant.io/news/defi/dromos-labs-merges-aerodrome-and-velodrome-into-new-dex-aero)) and from "September".

- 2026-09-16 — Aero Lite goes live on Circle's Arc L1 ([Aero](https://aero.xyz/articles/aero-lite-is-live-on-arc/)).

- 2026-09-25 — Launch date set for Oct 21, and Robinhood Chain and Arbitrum are added as launch chains ([Aero](https://aero.xyz/articles/aero-launch-update-all-systems-go/)).

- 2026-10-01 — Coinbase announces it will migrate AERO/VELO balances Nov 2–4 at no fee and wind down VELO trading ([Crypto Briefing](https://cryptobriefing.com/coinbase-aero-velo-token-migration/)).

- 2026-10-10 — Per Aero, Aerodrome's share of tokenized-stock DEX trading on Ethereum+L2s exceeds 50%, up from single digits in August.

- 2026-10-19 — "The Aero Economy" published: gauge caps (1.2x target), Momentum Fund, REV Engine ([Aero](https://aero.xyz/articles/the-aero-economy/)).

- 2026-10-22 00:00 UTC — Aero launches on 7 chains. Aerodrome/Velodrome emissions and gauges stop, new AERO emissions start, and the upgrade portals open ([Aero](https://aero.xyz/articles/aero-launches-today/); [The Block](https://www.theblock.co/news/defi/2026-10-21-aerodrome-velodrome-merge-aero-421514)).

- 2026-10-23 — New AERO all-time high of $0.7845 (CoinGecko).

- ~2026-11-01 (date unverified) — Autopilot (automated sAERO management) reported live. The feature is documented in the official docs ([docs: Autopilot](https://app.aero.xyz/docs/features/autopilot)), but the launch date could not be confirmed from a primary source; the CMC digest re-checked on 2026-11-10 no longer lists it.

- 2026-11-02 to 11-04 — Coinbase migration window.

- 2026-11-03 — Cumulative volume (including predecessors) nears $500B ([bsc.news via cryptonews.net](https://cryptonews.net/news/market/33692245/)).

- 2026-11-05 — AERO falls ~9–11% in 25h during a market-wide selloff, with no token-specific trigger identified ([CMC](https://coinmarketcap.com/top-stories/6aecd053186e1f6fb5ca129e/)).

- 2026-11-06 — A report relays social-media claims that Aero became the #2 DEX on Arbitrum within two weeks of launch, and says the ranking is hard to confirm ([CoinGabbar](https://www.coingabbar.com/en/aero-arbitrum-volume-dex-launch-ranking-claim)). Same day, Korean exchange Coinone announces a suspension of AERO deposits/withdrawals starting Nov 9 for the contract swap ([CMC news digest](https://coinmarketcap.com/cmc-ai/aerodrome-finance/latest-updates/)).

- 2026-11-08 — Crypto.com completes the AERO/VELO transition ([CMC news digest](https://coinmarketcap.com/cmc-ai/aerodrome-finance/latest-updates/)).

- 2026-11-09 — Aero on Elysium (Kinetiq's chain in the Hyperliquid ecosystem; listed among Aero deployments on the [security page](https://app.aero.xyz/docs/security/)): pools on "Elysium Kinetiq" first appear in DefiLlama fee data on this date ($596 fees on Nov 9; $13,957 on the partial day Nov 10). The Elysium mainnet date itself was not independently verified.

- Context (outside the 90-day window): Nov 21–22, 2025, a DNS hijack of the aerodrome.finance and velodrome.finance front-ends drained user approvals. Estimates range from ~$0.7M to more than $1M. The contracts were unaffected ([The Block](https://www.theblock.co/post/380037/top-dexs-aerodrome-velodrome-hit-with-front-end-compromise-urge-users-to-avoid-main-domains)). A similar incident happened in November 2023.

### Current problems and risks

- Revenue decline: quarterly exchange revenue fell from $111.2M (Q4 2024) to $16.4M (Q2 2026), a drop of about 85%, with $25.8M in Q3 2026 and Q4 2026 tracking about $21.9M (Aero's projection). DefiLlama monthly fees fell from $36.0M (Sep 2025) to $6.7–11.6M/month in Jan–Aug 2026, then $19.1M in Sep 2026 and $11.1M in Oct 2026 (sum of DefiLlama dailyFees by calendar month).

- Revenue quality: a majority of current holder revenue appears to be issuer-paid Liquidity/Launch Payments (bribes), not trader fees. Example: Sep 2026, $8.9M of $14.9M. Our on-chain sample of the top 25 Base pools shows small swap-fee flows. Bribe budgets are cyclical and depend on issuers' token prices and launches.

- Dilution vs. revenue: emissions of ~9.6%/yr, with the reward value (~$2.05M/week to LPs) currently above Aero's latest weekly revenue ($1.3M). The 20%/yr ceiling is still in the Minter. Gauge-cap multipliers and caps are set off-chain by multisigs, so issuance discipline depends on operator policy, not code.

- Price action: new AERO is −31% from its Oct 23 high (2026-11-10 15:55 UTC). Legacy AERO is −44% over 30d and −48% over 1y (CoinGecko, legacy id). The legacy ATH was $2.32 on 2024-12-07.

- Migration friction: ~373.0M AERO still unclaimed, and old pools still hold ~$120M TVL (37% of DefiLlama's $324.4M Aero-family TVL) without emissions. The Foundation plans to "reactivate" legacy gauges later to reclaim locked fees. Exchanges migrated on different timelines (Coinbase Nov 2–4, Crypto.com done Nov 8, Coinone from Nov 9), and CoinGecko still maps CEX markets to the legacy id, which creates data and liquidity fragmentation.

- Expansion so far is small: non-Base chains produced ~$0.34M of 7d holder revenue (Robinhood Chain $133k, Ethereum $124k, Arbitrum $43k, OP $26k; Nov 3–9) against $1.51M on Base (DefiLlama chain breakdown). Ethereum and Arbitrum launched with a 0% unstaked fee, so fee-earning LPs there pay sAERO nothing.

- Competition: Uniswap (v3/v4 hooks) holds 23% of Base volume, PancakeSwap 9%. Proprietary/RFQ AMMs (Tessera V, Hanji) are growing, and Aero itself names "Proprietary AMMs" as a threat to retail flow. CEX-like aggregator routing commoditizes venues.

- Centralization and admin keys: the Emergency Council can zero gauges and pause migration. Governance and operator multisigs control fee managers, the unstaked fee, swap-fee hooks, chain status and the team-share recipient list. Cross-chain emissions and messages rely on Hyperlane adapters (bridge risk). A SEIZER_ROLE exists for token-metadata NFTs.

- Operational and security history: two front-end DNS hijacks (Nov 2023, Nov 2025). The new MetaDEX03 code is about 3 weeks old in production, despite extensive audits and a $500k bounty.

- Concentration on Base and Coinbase: about 86% of TVL ($279.6M of $324.4M) and about 82% of 7d holder revenue ($1.51M of $1.85M, Nov 3–9) come from Base. A Base network token or Coinbase strategy changes could cut either way.

- Data quality: the official metrics page shows impossible "Cumulative Fees $68.87T", and aggregator per-pool volumes can be several times on-chain Swap totals (see §6).

What the bulls believe (hype case): Aero becomes the default venue where new on-chain asset classes list first: tokenized stocks (Coinbase B20, Robinhood Chain), FX stablecoins (EURC on Base/Arc), BTC (cbBTC), and new chains needing day-one liquidity (Arc, Elysium). The thesis is that paying LPs in a revenue-claim token lets Aero outbid rivals for liquidity, that dollar-denominated, capped rewards plus Momentum Fund burns make dilution self-correcting, and that "100% of revenue to stakers, no VCs" makes sAERO a clean cash-flow asset. Supporting evidence: 53% Base volume share, a claimed >50% tokenized-stock DEX share on 2026-10-10, $585M distributed lifetime, and 49.6% of supply staked with 89% of that in perpetual stakes.

### What would move the token

| Catalyst | Timing | Bullish if… | Bearish if… |

| --- | --- | --- | --- |

| Weekly exchange revenue vs. AERO emission value (Aero dashboard) | Weekly, every Thursday-dated week | Revenue sustainably > $2M/week while emissions stay ≤ ~4M AERO/week | Revenue stuck near $1–1.5M/week while emissions stay flat or rise |

| Momentum Fund buyback/burn activation | Undated; "market-aware" | Visible on-chain AERO/sAERO burns (transfers to the burn path / totalSupply reductions) | No burns while the price is in a drawdown |

| CEX migration completion and data remap (Binance, Upbit, Bithumb, Kraken, CoinGecko/CMC) | November 2026 (Coinone from Nov 9) | Smooth completion, consolidated liquidity | Delistings or extended deposit halts in Korea or elsewhere |

| Unclaimed migration supply (~373.0M) | Ongoing, no deadline | Claimed holders mostly stake (sAERO share rises above 50%) | Claimed tokens hit CEXs |

| Unstaked-fee increases on Base/OP; first Service Revenue (Metaswap fee, sAERO marketplace) | Not scheduled | Adds non-dilutive revenue | Delays |

| Tokenized stocks / Robinhood Chain growth, new Coinbase B20 listings | Rolling | Aero keeps >50% DEX share of tokenized-stock trading | Coinbase/Base routes flow to other venues or proprietary AMMs |

| Base network token | No date announced | Airdrop or incentives favouring Aero/Base DeFi | Incentives that subsidise competitors |

| Legacy gauge reactivation by the Foundation (to reclaim locked fees) | "At a later date" | — | Read as extra emissions |

| Security: first months of MetaDEX03 in production; DNS/front-end | Ongoing | No incidents | Any exploit, cross-chain messaging fault or front-end hijack |

