### Verification notes

Independent fact-check performed 2026-11-10 ~15:50–16:05 UTC by a second researcher who re-derived the key figures from primary sources rather than from the first draft.

#### Independently re-checked (confirmed)

- Contracts: AERO token, VotingEscrow (sAERO), Minter, AerodromeMigration, VelodromeMigrationEntrypoint, Splitter, Base CLFactory and DynamicSwapFeeHook addresses all match the official [security page](https://app.aero.xyz/docs/security/). On-chain name()/symbol() = "Aero"/"AERO"; the token's MINTER(), VOTING_ESCROW(), MIGRATION(), VELODROME_MIGRATION() pointers resolve to those addresses. Function selectors and the CollectFees/Swap event topics were recomputed from their signatures (keccak-256) and match.

- Supply/emissions: totalSupply, sAERO supply(), permanent stakes, NFT counter, Minter emissionsMinted(), baseRate() (13.489345 AERO/s), teamRate() (5%), ACTIVATION_TIMESTAMP (1792627200 = 2026-10-22 00:00 UTC), migration remaining()/paidBasis(), old AERO supply and old veAERO balance re-read on Base; VELO supply and veVELO balance re-read on OP Mainnet. All matched the draft within normal intraday drift; fresher values were substituted.

- Conversion terms (1:1 AERO; 0.044 AERO per VELO; 94.5%/5.5% split; ~12% expected realized inflation; 20% ceiling) confirmed on the [Upgrade Hub](https://aero.xyz/aero-upgrade/).

- Revenue: DefiLlama fees/revenue/holders-revenue 24h, 7d, 30d, 1y and all-time re-queried and identical to the draft; since-launch sums recomputed. Aero dashboard figures (lifetime $585M, quarterly series, week of Nov 5 $1.3M, emissions 3.91M AERO, 180.39M acquired/locked, TVL $309.27M, "$68.87T" cumulative-fees glitch) confirmed on the metrics page. Sept 2026 $14.9M = $6.1M + $8.9M vs $10.5M, the 1.2x target, the unstaked-fee rates by chain and the ~8% / ~11% issuance statements confirmed in [The Aero Economy](https://aero.xyz/articles/the-aero-economy/).

- On-chain cross-check of value flow: re-ran the WETH/USDC CL50 log scan over a fresh 24h window: CollectFees go to 0x623de2a4…fef48 (topics[1]), 2.1682 WETH + 2,283.10 USDC; 2,778 swaps, $8.46M USDC-leg volume; unstakedFee() = 5%. This confirms the draft's order of magnitude and its conclusion that blue-chip swap-fee capture is small relative to DefiLlama's holder revenue.

- Market data: CoinGecko (new and legacy ids), DefiLlama Base/OP DEX shares, TVL by chain and new-vs-legacy pool TVL, Binance and Bybit open interest re-queried.

- People: all names, titles and X handles in the Key people table confirmed on the [Dromos team page](https://dromos.xyz/).

- News links opened: Coinbase migration (announced Oct 1, window Nov 2–4), Sep 25 launch update (Oct 21 date; Robinhood Chain and Arbitrum added), Sep 16 Arc launch, Aug 24 tokenized stocks, Jul 16 security update ($400k contest, Mythos review), FXStreet −20% (2025-11-13), The Defiant (Q2 2026 original target), bsc.news via cryptonews.net (Nov 3), CMC Nov 5 selloff, CoinGabbar Arbitrum claim, CMC digest (Crypto.com Nov 8; Coinone announced Nov 6, effective Nov 9). The Block links returned HTTP 403 to automated fetches and were not re-opened.

- Format: all 13 required sections present in order; document in English; no API keys; no price predictions or probabilities.

#### Corrected

- Truncated contract addresses in §2 were wrong (Minter shown as "0x59268A34…cF", Velodrome migration as "0x6daE95FE…f666c0"); replaced with full verified addresses.

- Binance AERO perp funding interval is 4h, not 8h; OI and funding refreshed.

- Removed the Grayscale DeFi Fund removal claim: the cited KuCoin/AMBCrypto page does not mention Grayscale, and no other source was found.

- Base 7d holder revenue corrected from $1.54M to $1.51M (DefiLlama's total7d covers complete days Nov 3–9; $1.54M mixed in the partial Nov 10); non-Base share and Base concentration percentages adjusted.

- "DefiLlama monthly fees $7–11M through most of 2026" replaced with the exact monthly range, including the Sep 2026 spike ($19.1M).

- Sherlock contest dates "Aug 24 – Sep 11" were not supported by the cited source; replaced with "August–September 2026" per the security page. Autopilot launch date and Elysium mainnet date marked unverified; Coinone item given a source.

