As of 2026-11-10

Price snapshot: CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 15:43 UTC (refreshed by the fact-checker). On-chain reads: Ethereum blocks 26,385,135–26,385,513 (2026-11-10 ~14:30–15:50 UTC) via ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com and the Etherscan V2 API. DefiLlama pulls: 2026-11-10 14:32 UTC. Numbers in brackets such as [3] point to the Sources section.

### Executive summary

CRV is the governance and emissions token of Curve Finance, an Ethereum-first DEX built for assets that should trade near the same price, such as stablecoins, ETH derivatives and BTC wrappers. It also runs the crvUSD stablecoin and the Llamalend lending markets. Holders who lock CRV as veCRV do receive real cash flow. On-chain, the veCRV FeeDistributor paid $6.80M in crvUSD over the last 52 weeks and $615k over the last 4 complete weeks. That is 90% of the DAO's fee share; since July 2025 (first FeeAllocator distribution on 2025-07-02) the other 10% has gone to the DAO treasury. The cash flow is small next to the token: a $401M market cap is about 59x the trailing holder payouts, and CRV emissions are worth roughly $24.6M a year at today's price. The business is shrinking. TVL fell from $2.20B a year ago (2025-11-10) to $1.18B, and DefiLlama-counted monthly fees fell 43% year on year ($7.83M in Oct 2025 vs $4.47M in Oct 2026). CRV traded at $0.253 (2026-11-10 15:43 UTC) after a 31% drop over 30 days and set an all-time low of $0.171 on 2026-06-06. Current growth stories are Llamalend V2, which can take Curve LP tokens as collateral, non-EVM and stablecoin-chain deployments (Stellar, Arc) and FX pools. The single most important thing to watch is whether weekly veCRV distributions hold above about $150k once the post-Binance-hack volatility fades. A second item is the planned proposal to raise the treasury's fee share from 10% to 30%, which would cut veCRV's share from 90% to 70%.

### What the token is

- Ticker: CRV (Curve DAO Token). Canonical ERC-20 on Ethereum: 0xD533a949740bb3306d119CC777fa900bA034cd52, written in Vyper 0.2.4. Verified by calling totalSupply() and rate() on this address [4][1].

- Bridged representations (from the CoinGecko platform list; the Arbitrum, Optimism, Base and Polygon addresses were checked on-chain by the fact-checker on 2026-11-10 and return symbol() = "CRV"; Fantom and Etherlink not checked): Arbitrum 0x11cdb42b0eb46d95f990bedd4695a6e3fa034978, Optimism 0x0994206dfe8de6ec6920ff4d779b0d950605fb53, Base 0x8ee73c484a26e0a5df2ee2a4960b789967dd0415, Polygon 0x172370d5cd63279efa6d502dab29171933a610af, Fantom 0x1e4f97b9f9f913c46f1632781732927b9019c68b, Etherlink 0x004a476b5b76738e34c86c7144554b9d34402f13 [2]. Governance and veCRV exist only on Ethereum [9].

- veCRV: VotingEscrow contract 0x5f3b5DfEb7B28CDbD7FAba78963EE202a494e2A2. veCRV is non-transferable. Locks run from 1 week to 4 years, and voting power decays linearly toward unlock [9][10].

