#### Issuance schedule and unlocks

- Emissions follow a fixed, immutable schedule in the token contract. Each epoch lasts one year, and at each new epoch the rate is divided by 2^(1/4), a cut of about 15.9% that halves the rate every 4 years. Anyone can trigger the change by calling update_mining_parameters(); no vote is needed [4][13].

- Epoch history (CRV per year): epoch 0 (2020–21) 274.8M; epoch 1 231.1M; epoch 2 194.3M; epoch 3 163.4M; epoch 4 137.4M; epoch 5 115.5M; epoch 6 (2026-08-12 to 2027-08-12) 97.16M; epoch 7 (from about 2027-08-12) about 81.7M (estimate: 97.16M / 1.189) [13]. The on-chain mining_epoch() returns 6, and start_epoch_time() = 1786573048 = 2026-08-12 22:17:28 UTC.

- Emitted CRV goes to liquidity gauges, and veCRV votes decide the split (1,052 gauges registered in GaugeController 0x2F50D538606Fa9EDD2B11E2446BEb18C9D5846bB, on-chain n_gauges()).

- No team or VC cliff unlocks remain. At genesis, 62% of the 3.03B maximum was reserved for liquidity providers and released as emissions. The rest was allocated to shareholders (team and investors, about 30%, vesting 2–4 years), employees (about 3%, 2 years) and a community reserve (about 5%). This allocation comes from Curve's original token documentation and was not re-verified on-chain here. All shareholder and employee vesting ended by August 2024. The remaining sources of new supply are gauge emissions and DAO-approved grants.

- DAO-approved CRV grants that are vesting or recently vested (potential sell flow): 17.45M CRV to Swiss Stake AG for 2026, in two 8.725M halves (votes 1297, executed Dec 2025, and 1381, executed Apr 2026). Also 3.75M CRV to the Curve Grants multisig (vote 1381), 568,181 CRV over 1 year to yRisk (vote 1492, Aug 2026), 2.5M CRV plus 360k crvUSD over 1 year to LlamaRisk (vote 1363; vote 1441, executed 2026-06-30, revoked only the unvested crvUSD stream, and the status of the 2.5M CRV stream was not confirmed), and up to 5M CRV through a veFunder gauge for sDOLA exploit victims (vote 1437, June 2026) [15].

