| (b'') Treasury share, on-chain (FeeAllocator events) | $167.7k from 2026-08-12 to 2026-11-04 (10% of $1,676,694 distributed) |  |  |  | Etherscan logs, FeesDistributed |

| (c) Reaching veCRV holders, on-chain FeeDistributor tokens_per_week | n/a (weekly) | $269,092 (week starting 2026-10-29) | $614,990 (4 weeks starting 2026-10-08 → 11-04) | $6,803,535 (52 weeks, 2025-11-06 → 2026-11-04); 13-week run-rate $1,507,971 × 4 = $6.03M | On-chain eth_call; matches prices.curve.finance /v1/dao/fees/distributions [5] |

| (c') DefiLlama "HoldersRevenue" (90% admin + all bribes) | $195.5k | $969.6k | $2.75M | $25.6M | DefiLlama dailyHoldersRevenue [3] |

Why DefiLlama's holder number is about 4x the on-chain number. (1) DefiLlama's Curve methodology counts all bribes to veCRV voters as holders revenue [3]. Those incentives (about $259k/week [6]) go mostly to Convex/vlCVX voters, not pro rata to veCRV, and are paid by third parties, not Curve users. (2) DefiLlama books fees on the day they are earned. The on-chain distribution lags 1–2 weeks because of the CowSwap burn and the weekly epoch: on 2026-11-10 (15:45 UTC), 71,887 crvUSD sat in the FeeDistributor and 130,073 crvUSD in the FeeCollector, waiting to be distributed. The Oct 29 – Nov 5 volatility fees will appear in the next weekly epochs. (3) DefiLlama's DEX fee count appears to include high-fee Yield Basis pool fees that have admin_fee() = 0 and never reach the DAO. This is an inference from the on-chain pool reads; the DefiLlama adapter was not audited line by line. For value accrual to an ordinary veCRV holder, use row (c).

