As of 2026-11-10

### Executive summary

1INCH is the fixed-supply (1.5B, mint permanently disabled) ERC-20 governance token of the 1inch DAO, which governs the open-source protocols (Aggregation Router, Limit Order Protocol, Fusion/Fusion+, and since July 2026 Aqua/SwapVM) behind the 1inch DEX aggregator. In practice the company that runs the product is Degensoft, the private 1inch operating group led by Sergej Kunz. Since 1IP-88 (Sept 2025) it owns the 1inch.com dApp and its fee revenue: infrastructure fees and swap surplus.

No value reaches token holders today. DefiLlama's holders revenue is $0 for every period. The DAO's only protocol income is a small Aqua fee share: about $8.4K–8.6K in the last 30 days and about $37.4K since 2026-07-19 (DefiLlama), which on-chain reads corroborate: the Ethereum Aqua FeeCollector has delivered 34,986.93 USDC to the DAO Treasury in 21 transfers (2026-09-23 to 2026-11-10 15:43 UTC). On a $104.7M market cap (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 15:44 UTC), that is roughly 1,000x annualized DAO revenue.

The state is weak. Aggregator volume on DefiLlama fell about 90% from mid-2025 peaks to about $3B/month. The token is down 64% year on year and about 15% above its all-time low. The 5% staking requirement for resolvers was removed in Oct 2025, and a July 2026 forum post (unanswered) says delegators no longer receive resolver rewards. Co-founder Anton Bukov left after a public dispute. On 2026-10-29/30, about 19.0M 1INCH taken from Binance in the $6.3B hack were dumped on-chain.

The single thing to watch is whether Aqua (the shared-liquidity protocol whose fee share goes to the DAO) builds real fee-paying volume once incentives end, and whether the DAO ever routes value to holders. Aqua volume fell from about $228M in August to about $2M in the last 7 days after Season 1 incentives ended on 2026-10-27.

### What the token is

- Ticker / name: 1INCH ("1INCH Token"). CoinGecko id 1inch, market-cap rank #254 (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 15:44 UTC).

- Canonical contract (Ethereum): 0x111111111117dC0aa78b770fA6A738034120C302. This is the OneInch contract (Solidity 0.6.12, ERC20Permit + ERC20Burnable + Ownable). It has a mint() function, but owner() returns 0x0 (I read it via eth_call on 2026-11-10), so no new tokens can ever be minted. The 1.5B supply was minted in the constructor (Dec 2020).

