- Team Investment Fund activity (my on-chain read of the fund's 1INCH transfers): it bought on the open market in 2024–2025. Media citing on-chain trackers report about $7.5M spent for about 37.3M 1INCH at about $0.20 in July 2025. It took in a further 33.6M 1INCH in Nov 2025 and 25.0M in Jan–Feb 2026, mostly withdrawals from Binance. On 2026-07-23 it sent 37.5M 1INCH to Safe 0x3fbc2bee…fb85, which on 2026-07-30 bridged 37.499M to Robinhood Chain through the Robinhood Chain L1ERC20Gateway 0x85001cc4…6da0 (not Arbitrum, as an earlier draft said; the gateway's L2 token is the Robinhood Chain 1INCH contract). On Robinhood Chain the same Safe address holds 39.26M 1INCH (RPC read, 2026-11-10). On Ethereum it keeps 1.11M 1INCH and shows Aqua maker activity (fills paying the DAO fee into the Aqua FeeCollector since 2026-08-14). The purpose has not been officially disclosed; the timing coincides with Aqua Season 1, which rewarded 1INCH-paired markets.

### How it works

#### The product (for users)

- Classic swap (Aggregation Router v6, 0x111111125421cA6dc452d289314280a0f8842A65): the Pathfinder engine splits an order across hundreds of DEX pools on 18+ chains. The user signs and pays gas.

- Fusion (intent swaps): the user signs an off-chain order, and a Dutch auction lets whitelisted "resolvers" (professional market makers) compete to fill it. Resolvers pay the gas. The user receives at least the auction price. Fusion+ extends this to atomic cross-chain swaps (EVM↔EVM and EVM↔Solana) using hashlock/timelock escrows, with no bridge.

- Limit Order Protocol (LOP): on-chain settlement of signed limit orders. It is also the settlement layer for Fusion.

- Aqua + SwapVM (dev release 2025-11-17, production launch 2026-07-19 to 07-28): "shared liquidity". LPs keep funds in their own wallets and publish programmable strategies (SwapVM bytecode: AMM curves, PMM, fees). The same capital can back several strategies. Taker fills are routed via the AquaRouter 0x1111113ccf1426a8e30e2bff5e005d929bf6a90a (same address on every chain). The code is source-available under the "Degensoft Aqua Source License 1.1", not under an OSI open-source license.

- Other products (not DAO-owned): 1inch Wallet, Portfolio, the 1inch Business API portal (paid plans plus x402 pay-per-call), and the 1inch Card, which is being wound down by 2026-12-18.

#### The token mechanics

- Staking (st1INCH, 0x9A0C8Ff858d273f57072D714bca7411D717501D7): users lock 1INCH for 30 to 730 days (MIN_LOCK_PERIOD = 2,592,000 s; MAX_LOCK_PERIOD = 63,072,000 s; on-chain read). Locking gives "Unicorn Power" (UP), which decays exponentially toward unlock. UP is voting power on Snapshot (space 1inch.eth) and can be delegated to resolvers. Early withdrawal is allowed with a penalty (maxLossRatio = 90%). Penalties go to feeReceiver() = the DAO Treasury 0x7951…1c07 (on-chain read). Total locked: 235,549,114 1INCH (totalDeposits(), 2026-11-10).

- Resolver access: resolvers originally had to hold at least 5% of total UP, delegated by stakers, to receive Fusion's exclusive order flow (1IP-33/43). 1IP-89 (passed 2025-10-21) removed this threshold. Access now depends on KYC/due diligence and a Resolver NFT administered by 1inch Business. Resolver "farms" that paid delegators remain optional. A user forum post on 2026-07-03 (no official reply as of 2026-11-10) says delegators are no longer receiving resolver incentives; I could not confirm this on-chain.

- No buyback, burn or fee share to holders. The DAO stopped collecting aggregator swap surplus in Q2 2023. Swap surplus and infrastructure fees now go to the API-provider layer, 1inch Business (Degensoft).

- Aqua protocol fee (1IP-103, live since 2026-07-19): it takes 1/4 of the LP fee on low tiers (below about 0.1225%) and 1/6 on higher tiers. It is collected per fill to a FeeCollector beacon proxy (Ethereum: 0x8063d4faf54bf8c898dc6ddc689c76ab12b4614a), swapped to USDC, and sent to the DAO Treasury. Nothing goes to stakers or holders.

- Governance: Snapshot votes with UP. Execution is by the DAO Treasury Safe (7-of-12, ratified as the "Security Council" by 1IP-106 on 2026-09-19) via the SafeSnap/Reality module with a 72h timelock. The 1inch Foundation is the DAO's off-chain representative.

### Utility

- Real utility today: (1) DAO voting via st1INCH/UP. The DAO controls a treasury of about $4.5M, Aqua protocol-fee parameters, resolver access rules and grants. (2) Optional delegation to resolvers, which is economically minor now that the UP threshold is gone and rewards are reportedly paused. (3) Collateral and trading pair: it is listed on major CEXs, used in DEX pools, and was used as Aqua Season-1 1INCH-paired incentive markets.

- Not needed for: swapping on 1inch (users pay in any token; Fusion is gasless), paying API fees (USD plans or USDC via x402), Aqua LP or taker activity, or receiving any protocol cash flow. Since 1IP-89, resolvers no longer need it either.

- Assessment: 1INCH is essentially governance-only, and its governance does not control the main revenue lines (the dApp, API fees and surplus), which belong to Degensoft under 1IP-88. The official token page still says resolvers use 1INCH "to obtain and prioritize access". That is outdated relative to 1IP-89.

### Why people buy and sell it

#### Demand drivers

- Brand and beta exposure to DEX aggregation and "DeFi blue chips". It is listed on Binance, Coinbase, OKX, Bybit and others. KuCoin removed it from cross-margin on 2026-01-27.

- Narratives: RWA and tokenized-stock routing (Robinhood Chain launch partner on 2026-07-01, Ondo stocks on Solana on 2026-10-20, RWA Swap API on 2026-10-23); the Aqua "shared liquidity" thesis; a future DAO value-capture story (Aqua fees, possible resolver access fees under 1IP-89, LP fees).

- Team Investment Fund open-market buying in 2024–2025. It is a visible bid, but the fund also sold in Dec 2024 (about 19.6M out) and Feb/Jul 2025.

- Low price and about $105M market cap attract mean-reversion and speculative traders.

#### Supply and sell pressure

- No emissions and no large scheduled unlocks (about 19.2M still vesting in small steps). Overhang comes from large discretionary holders: the Team Investment Fund (106.8M), unlabeled whales (123.7M, 82.2M, 69.0M), the 1inch Foundation multisig (42.0M), 37.5M moved by the fund to Robinhood Chain in July 2026, 37.5M vested-but-unclaimed in the 2020 StepVesting contracts, and about 19.2M still vesting in smaller contracts through 2031.

- Incentive tokens: the Foundation funded 10M 1INCH for Aqua LP rewards (Season 1) and offers "$250k in 1INCH" for Season 2. Recipients tend to sell.

- Hack dump: about 19.03M 1INCH (1.35% of circulating) was taken from Binance and sold on-chain on 2026-10-30 (see News). The token has no freeze function.

- Fundamental drag: falling aggregator volume, no holder yield, and an ongoing DAO treasury burn on grants, events and incentives.

### The protocol/business

- What it does: it is a DEX aggregator and intent-based execution layer, launched in 2019 at ETHGlobal. Volume comes from three sources: the retail dApp and wallet, B2B API integrations (wallets, exchanges and dApps use the 1inch Swap/Fusion APIs), and resolver-filled intent orders. The strategy shift since late 2025 is toward B2B infrastructure (a "we are the swap" rebrand), RWA/tokenized stocks, and the Aqua liquidity layer.

- Organizational structure: (1) 1inch DAO: governance, staking, protocol contracts and treasury (1inch.network). (2) 1inch Foundation (reported Cayman entity; not re-verified): the DAO's off-chain representative, which administers grants and the Aqua Incubator. (3) Degensoft Ltd (developer: DIFC, UAE; operator: BVI), branded "1inch" / "1inch Business": owns and operates the 1inch.com dApp since 1IP-88 (passed 2025-09-27) and develops the protocols, wallet and APIs. It is the licensor of Aqua/SwapVM.

- Chains: per DefiLlama, aggregator volume covers 19 chains: Ethereum, BSC, Polygon, Arbitrum, OP, Avalanche, Gnosis, Fantom, Sonic, zkSync, Base, Linea, Solana, Unichain, Robinhood Chain, Monad, Hyperliquid L1, Arc and Cronos. Volume is concentrated on Ethereum: $31.4M of $44.5M (70.6%) on 2026-11-09 (latest full day in DefiLlama). Next are Base ($3.9M), BSC ($3.1M) and Arbitrum ($3.0M).

- Users: DeFi power users and whales on Ethereum, wallets and exchanges via the API, market-maker resolvers, and, more recently, RWA traders on Robinhood Chain and Solana. The 1inch.network page states 137k+ token holders.

- Market share (DefiLlama aggregator volume, 30d to 2026-11-09):

