| OKX Swap | $4.87B | $0.76B | 3.6% |

| Uniswap Aggregator | $3.38B | $2.72B | 12.7% |

| CoW Swap | $3.35B | $3.03B | 14.2% |

| 1inch Swap | $2.80B (#8; 4.4% of $64.03B) | $2.33B (#5) | 10.9% |

| Bebop | $1.96B | $1.34B | 6.3% |

| Velora (ex-ParaSwap) | $1.75B | $1.40B | 6.5% |

- Volume trend (DefiLlama 1inch-swap monthly totals): 2025-05 $34.0B, 2025-06 $38.8B, 2025-09 $21.9B, 2025-12 $6.0B, 2026-03 $4.2B, 2026-07 $2.6B, 2026-10 $3.5B. 1-year total: $47.7B. All-time on DefiLlama: $803B. Note that DefiLlama's adapter now uses the 1inch-maintained Dune spellbook with dedup rules, so absolute levels may differ from 1inch's own figures. The direction (a decline of roughly 90% from the mid-2025 peak) matches press reports of an "81% volume drop" around July 2026.

- Aqua: volume $339.7M all-time. Monthly: Aug $227.8M, Sep $29.6M, Oct $75.2M. Last 7d to 2026-11-09: $2.07M; daily: $0.25M on 2026-11-09 and $0.16M on 2026-11-10 (DefiLlama 1inch-aqua, read 2026-11-10 ~15:50 UTC). Per a delegate analysis on the Season 2 thread (Arana Digital, 2026-11-04), Ethereum produced about 90% of Aqua's 30-day volume. Live on 15 chains, including Ethereum, Arbitrum, BSC, Base, Robinhood Chain and Arc.

- Key integrations and partners: Robinhood Chain launch partner (2026-07-01, about 100 tokenized stocks, Classic + Fusion); Ondo Global Markets on Solana (2026-10-20); Circle's Arc L1 (2026-09-16); Cronos (2026-09-10); BNB Chain as Aqua co-incentive partner; Merkl for reward distribution; zeroShadow, SEAL 911 and TRM for risk and blocklists.

### Revenue and value capture

#### (a) Gross fees paid by users

- Aggregator, Fusion and API: the fee base consists of infrastructure fees and swap surplus. Infrastructure fees (1inch Business FAQ) are 2–10 bps on stablecoins and 5–30 bps on other assets depending on API plan. 1inch's own interfaces may charge 0–5 bps on stable pairs and 0–30 bps on others. Swap surplus (positive slippage) "is retained by the API provider (1inch Business)" (help center, 2026-10-09). No public, verified figure for this revenue exists. DefiLlama does not track it. DL News (2025-08-19) reported "$5.3 million in annual revenue" that 1inch Labs and the Foundation declined to share with the DAO. The figure comes from the Arana/StableLab proposal (forum 821), which annualized $893,415.65 of Fusion surplus and limit-order taker fees observed over two months in mid-2025. It is an unaudited, 15-month-old estimate, and aggregator volume has fallen about 90% since.

- Aqua (DefiLlama 1inch-aqua adapter, decoded per fill from SwapVM fee opcodes):

| Aqua metric (USD) | Day 2026-11-09 | 7d to 11-09 | 30d to 11-09 | Since 2026-07-19 (to 11-10) | Annualized (30d×12.17) |

| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |

| Total fees (LP + DAO) | 1,773 | 13,350 | 42,264 | 187,780 | about 514,000 (estimate) |

| Protocol revenue = DAO fee share | 417 | 2,896 | 8,410 | 37,447 | about 102,000 (estimate) |

| Holders revenue | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |

DefiLlama had also published a 2026-11-10 data point at read time (~15:50 UTC; may be partial): fees $1,271, DAO revenue $308; the rolling 30d to 11-10 is $42,999 fees / $8,608 revenue. The API's total24h/total7d/total30d fields were still keyed to 11-09 for the parent slug 1inch but to 11-10 for 1inch-aqua, which is why the two slugs can show different "24h" numbers. Aqua DAO revenue by month: Jul $1.6K, Aug $9.4K, Sep $11.1K, Oct $11.5K, Nov 1–10 $3.7K. Fee revenue stayed flat even as volume fell. This suggests that much of the incentivized Season-1 volume was zero- or low-fee volume, a point a delegate raised on the Season 2 thread.

#### (b) Protocol revenue (DAO)

- Aqua DAO fee: see the table above. It is cross-checked on-chain: the Ethereum FeeCollector 0x8063d4fa…614a sent 21 USDC transfers totalling 34,986.93 USDC to the DAO Treasury between 2026-09-23 and 2026-11-10 (latest: 1,056.22 USDC at 15:43 UTC on 2026-11-10, which emptied the collector's USDC balance). In the 30 days 2026-10-11 to 2026-11-10 it sent 8,493.12 USDC, against DefiLlama's $8,410–8,608 for all chains. Differences come from batching and conversion timing (transfers are roughly weekly, about $1K each) and from other chains' collectors. No Ethereum transfers appear before 2026-09-23 even though fees accrued from 2026-07-19, so earlier fees were either batched into the first two large transfers (8,704 and 9,555 USDC on 09-23/09-25) or routed differently; I did not resolve this. Both sources agree on the order of magnitude: about $100K a year.

- st1INCH early-unlock penalties: 1,944.56 1INCH (about $145) reached the treasury in 9 transfers from 2026-08-03 to 2026-10-12 (Etherscan transfers from st1INCH to the treasury).

- Treasury yield: 2.73M aEthUSDC on Aave v3 (1IP-92, March 2026). On 2026-08-12, 500K aEthUSDC was moved out for the Aqua Season-1 USDC budget.

- Uniswap V3 1INCH/WETH LP fees: about $112.8K uncollected (snapshot of 2026-09-16), proposal 1000. This is a one-off, not recurring.

#### (c) What reaches token holders

Nothing. There is no buyback, burn, staking yield from fees, or distribution. Money flows go DAO Treasury → grants, incentives and service providers. Example: Aqua LP Season 2 (proposal of 2026-10-30) asks for 250K USDC from the DAO plus $250K in 1INCH from the Foundation over 13 weeks. That is about $38.5K a week of incentives, against about $2–3K a week of DAO fee revenue.

#### Stated monetization plans

- 1IP-103 says protocol fees go to the treasury and can be retuned by governance. Degensoft intends to propose a separate "Development & Service Fee" framework (partly in 1INCH with vesting), which would be a new treasury outflow.

- 1IP-89 says "Resolver Access Fees can be enabled", with allocation (DAO or others) to be decided later. Not active.

- Aqua Revenue Stream Incubator (1IP-93): $400K in grants to strategy teams (Aqua0, Bleu, Steer, 1delta) with revenue-share obligations to the DAO. No revenue reported yet.

- The 2025 "Financial Revitalization" proposal (Arana and StableLab) would have redirected Fusion surplus and limit-order taker fees to the DAO. Labs and the Foundation rejected it, and it was superseded by the dApp transfer (1IP-88) and the Aqua fee.

### How to verify on-chain

Values below were obtained on 2026-11-10 (Ethereum blocks 26,385,199 to 26,385,493, about 14:40–15:50 UTC) and re-run by the fact-checker. Load your own Etherscan key into $ETHERSCAN_API_KEY. Never paste keys into documents.

#### 1. Supply, mint authority, staking

# totalSupply() of 1INCH -> 1,499,999,999.997 (divide hex result by 1e18)curl -s https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0x111111111117dC0aa78b770fA6A738034120C302","data":"0x18160ddd"},"latest"]}'# owner() -> 0x000...000 (mint disabled)  ... same call with "data":"0x8da5cb5b"# st1INCH totalDeposits() -> 235,549,114.2 1INCH locked  ... "to":"0x9A0C8Ff858d273f57072D714bca7411D717501D7","data":"0x7d882097"# st1INCH feeReceiver() -> 0x7951c7ef839e26f63da87a42c9a87986507f1c07 (DAO Treasury)  ... "data":"0xb3f00674"

#### 2. DAO Treasury balances (Safe 0x7951c7ef839e26F63DA87a42C9a87986507f1c07)

# balanceOf(treasury) on 1INCH / USDC / aEthUSDCDATA=0x70a082310000000000000000000000007951c7ef839e26f63da87a42c9a87986507f1c07for T in 0x111111111117dC0aa78b770fA6A738034120C302 0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48 0x98C23E9d8f34FEFb1B7BD6a91B7FF122F4e16F5c; do curl -s https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \  -d "{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"eth_call\",\"params\":[{\"to\":\"$T\",\"data\":\"$DATA\"},\"latest\"]}"; done

Reads at block 26,385,493 (2026-11-10 ~15:45 UTC): 4,651,180.9 1INCH; 35,885.96 USDC (34,829.74 before the 15:43 UTC Aqua fee transfer); 2,729,960.86 aEthUSDC (interest-bearing, grows each block); 257.53 ETH (eth_getBalance). Safe getThreshold() = 7, getOwners() length = 12. DefiLlama's treasury view (api.llama.fi/treasury/1inch) shows about $4.16M of non-native assets on Ethereum (aEthUSDC $2.73M, WETH $1.05M, WBTC $0.14M, DAI $0.13M, USDT $0.08M), plus $0.35M in own 1INCH and $23K USDC on Arbitrum. Total: about $4.54M.

#### 3. Aqua DAO fee flow (protocol revenue)

# USDC Transfer logs FeeCollector(0x8063d4fa...) -> DAO Treasury, since AquaRouter deploy block 25555262curl -s "https://api.etherscan.io/v2/api?chainid=1&module=logs&action=getLogs&address=0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48&fromBlock=25555262&toBlock=latest&topic0=0xddf252ad1be2c89b69c2b068fc378daa952ba7f163c4a11628f55a4df523b3ef&topic0_1_opr=and&topic1=0x0000000000000000000000008063d4faf54bf8c898dc6ddc689c76ab12b4614a&topic1_2_opr=and&topic2=0x0000000000000000000000007951c7ef839e26f63da87a42c9a87986507f1c07&apikey=$ETHERSCAN_API_KEY" \ \ | python3 -c "import sys,json;r=json.load(sys.stdin)['result'];print(len(r),sum(int(x['data'],16) for x in r)/1e6,'USDC')"# Result (2026-11-10 15:50 UTC): 21 logs, sum 34,986.93 USDC; first 2026-09-23, last 2026-11-10 15:43 UTC.# Pending in collector: balanceOf(0x8063d4fa...) on USDC = 0.000001 USDC right after that sweep (951.77 earlier the same day)

The FeeCollector is a BeaconProxy with an implementation named FeeCollector (0x544e62df…6569). Every Aqua fill on Ethereum pushes the DAO share of the input token to it, and it converts that to USDC. On other chains, the per-chain collector is encoded in each strategy (SwapVM opcode 27/28 argument to). See the DefiLlama adapter fees/oneinch-aqua.ts.

#### 4. Aggregator data (DefiLlama, Snapshot)

curl -s "https://api.llama.fi/summary/fees/1inch?dataType=dailyHoldersRevenue" | jq '.total24h,.total30d,.totalAllTime'   # 0,0,0curl -s "https://api.llama.fi/summary/fees/1inch-aqua?dataType=dailyRevenue" | jq '.totalDataChart[-3:]'  # [11-08,224],[11-09,417],[11-10,308]curl -s "https://api.llama.fi/summary/aggregators/1inch?dataType=dailyVolume" | jq '.total24h,.total30d,.total1y'      # 44.5M, 2.80B, 47.7Bcurl -s "https://api.llama.fi/summary/dexs/1inch-aqua?dataType=dailyVolume" | jq '.totalDataChart[-2:]'      # 11-09 254,073; 11-10 164,278curl -s https://hub.snapshot.org/graphql -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"query":"{proposals(first:10,where:{space:\"1inch.eth\"},orderBy:\"created\",orderDirection:desc){title state scores}}"}'

