### Key people

- Sergej Kunz: co-founder and CEO of 1inch (Degensoft group); public face and strategy ([@deacix](https://x.com/deacix)). He remains in charge after Bukov's exit.

- Anton Bukov: co-founder and former CTO and lead smart-contract architect ([@k06a](https://x.com/k06a)). Departed. He says he was "fired" in Nov 2025. 1inch says he was not an employee and has not contributed since Dec 2025. He announced a new company, Second Tier, on 2026-07-16 and says he retains a 50% equity stake in the company.

- Holly Atkinson: Chief Product & Technology Officer since 2026-07-07 (formerly The Sandbox, Boson Protocol). Leads product, including the Aqua rollout.

- George Evans: Head of Product Design since 2026-07-07.

- Hedi Navazan: Chief Compliance Officer (reported appointment Nov 2024; current status not verified, no source re-checked for this document).

- 1inch Foundation: described in earlier reporting as a Cayman Islands foundation company (not re-verified; the foundation page does not state its jurisdiction). It controls a multisig (0x5E89f8d8…D7D1, 41.99M 1INCH per Blockscout label). Its directors are not publicly named. It signs as "1inch_Foundation" on the forum and administers resolver onboarding (delegated to 1inch Business), the Aqua Incubator and grants. Jordan Reindl has been cited as the 1inch Labs governance lead (DL News, 2025).

- DAO delegates and service providers: DAOplomats (author of 1IP-103 and the LP-fee collection draft, forum #1000), Anode / Kene (Aqua incentive programs, Incubator steward), RoundElephant, Arana Digital and StableLab (authors of the 2025 revenue proposal), FranklinDAO, PGov, MME (external counsel, 1IP-94), and the Legal Working Group.

- Official accounts: [@1inch](https://x.com/1inch); governance hub 1inch.network; forum gov.1inch.network.

### Recent news (last ~90 days)

- 2026-11-10: latest Aqua FeeCollector → Treasury transfer of 1,056.22 USDC at 15:43 UTC (on-chain; previous 1,049.54 USDC on 2026-11-05).

- 2026-11-01 to 11-04: delegate feedback on Season 2 ([forum 1027](https://gov.1inch.network/t/1027)): RoundElephant flagged that rewards (~$38.5K/week) against a day-30 fee gate of ~$3.4K/week make two-wallet wash trading profitable; Arana Digital computed that eligible fees would need about $154K/week for the program to pay for itself, roughly 12x October's $54.5K of Aqua fees across all chains.

- 2026-10-30: [Aqua LP Incentive Program Season 2](https://gov.1inch.network/t/1027) proposed: 250K USDC (DAO) plus $250K in 1INCH (Foundation), 13 weeks from 2026-11-10 at the earliest. Rewards are paid on LP fees rather than volume, across 20 Ethereum pairs.

- 2026-10-29/30: the [$6.36B Binance hack](https://www.trmlabs.com/resources/blog/north-korea-steals-usd-6-36-billion-from-binance-in-the-largest-hack-in-history) (TRM attributes it to the DPRK TraderTraitor group). 1inch blocklisted attacker addresses across dApp, wallet and API within one hour ([TokenPost](https://www.tokenpost.com/news/technology/44295)). 1INCH was among the stolen assets and cannot be frozen. The token fell 13% ([TokenPost](https://www.tokenpost.com/news/investing/44872)). My on-chain trace: 19.03M 1INCH left Binance 14 at 20:24 UTC and was sold into a Uniswap V3 pool on 2026-10-30 at 01:47–01:55 UTC. Attribution of that address to the attacker is my inference from timing and pattern; I found no public label for it. Elliptic reports the attacker also used 1inch, Uniswap and RFQ makers to swap 434M USDT into ETH.

- 2026-10-27: Aqua Season 1 ended. A proposal to reallocate $200K of unused Incubator grants to a security-audit pool; four teams approved (Aqua0, Bleu, Steer, 1delta), and intake paused since 2026-09-17.

- 2026-10-23: RWA swaps via the 1inch Swap API (Ondo, xStocks, Maple, Coinbase-issued assets).

- 2026-10-20: Ondo tokenized stocks and ETFs available on Solana through 1inch. The 1inch Card wind-down was announced: no new sign-ups, and balances should be withdrawn by 2026-12-18.

- 2026-10-12: TokenPost reported open issues (since 2026-07-22) with clear-signing displays for swaps, orders and approvals.

- 2026-09-24: [draft proposal](https://gov.1inch.network/t/1006) to fund a 2-of-3 Governance Defense Safe with 2.5 ETH to counter malicious proposals on the DAO's Reality (SafeSnap) module.

- 2026-09-22: proposal to collect about $112.8K in accrued fees on the DAO's 1INCH/WETH Uniswap V3 LP (NFT #501891, out of range).

- 2026-09-19: 1IP-106 passed (28.05M UP for, 0 against): the 1inch DAO Security Council was established and 7 of 12 treasury signers were rotated.

- 2026-09-16 / 09-10: 1inch launched on Circle's Arc and on Cronos.

- 2026-08-05 / 08-03: 1IP-105 passed (500K USDC Aqua maker incentives). 1IP-104 passed (SEAL Safe Harbor adopted).

- 2026-07-28: Aqua public launch on 13 EVM chains, with 10M 1INCH (Foundation) plus 500K USDC (DAO) in LP rewards via Merkl ([The Defiant](https://thedefiant.io/news/defi/1inch-commits-10m-1inch-500k-usdc-to-aqua-lp-rewards)). The DAO fee went live from 2026-07-19 (2026-07-21 on BSC and Robinhood Chain), under 1IP-103.

- 2026-07-16: Anton Bukov's exit and dispute made public ([Cointelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/news/1inch-co-founder-not-involved-company)).

### Current problems and risks

- No value accrual to holders. Holders revenue is $0. Commercial cash flows (infrastructure fees and surplus) sit with private Degensoft by DAO vote (1IP-88), with "no current plans for fee sharing". The DAO earns about $100K a year from Aqua against a $104.7M market cap.

- Utility erosion. 1IP-89 removed the 5% UP staking requirement for resolvers, eliminating the main structural reason to lock 1INCH. Delegator rewards reportedly stopped (user forum post, 2026-07-03, unanswered).

- Volume decline and share loss. DefiLlama monthly volume fell from $38.8B (Jun 2025) to $3.5B (Oct 2026). 1inch ranks #8 overall and #5 on Ethereum (10.9%), behind KyberSwap, CoW, 0x and Uniswap's aggregator. Solana aggregators (Jupiter, DFlow) dominate total flow.

- Aqua traction is unproven. Volume collapsed after incentives ended: $2.07M in the last 7d versus $66.3M over 30d. Incentive spend ($38.5K a week proposed) far exceeds DAO fee income ($2–3K a week). Delegates flagged wash-trading risk in the reward design.

- DAO treasury runway. The treasury is about $4.5M. Large historical outflows include about $2.24M on events, $2.0M on a hardware-wallet grant that never shipped a 1inch-branded product (settled via 1IP-95), $1.98M on the Bruce Lee campaign, and $0.77M in hack reimbursements. In Aug 2025 delegates estimated about 2 years of runway. A Degensoft service-fee proposal is pending.

- Centralization and IP. Aqua/SwapVM are source-available under a Degensoft license, the dApp and domain belong to Degensoft, and resolver onboarding is KYC-gated by 1inch Business.

- Governance and people. A public co-founder dispute: Bukov claims a 50% equity stake and has started a new venture. The Foundation's directors are not disclosed.

- Security history. In March 2025 a resolver using deprecated Fusion v1 was exploited for about $5M; most was returned after a bounty of about $450K. There was also an Oct 2026 clear-signing display issue. The token has no freeze capability, so stolen supply can always be dumped.

- Overhang. Non-exchange, non-staking wallets hold more than 500M 1INCH (Team Investment Fund 106.8M, unlabeled 123.7M, 82.2M, 69.0M and 40.0M, 1inch Foundation multisig 42.0M, plus 39.26M on Robinhood Chain in the Safe funded by the Team Fund). None of these is locked.

- Market structure. KuCoin removed cross-margin support (2026-01-27). The price ($0.0745 on 2026-11-10) is about 15% above its all-time low ($0.0649 on 2026-07-01).

What bulls point to: RWA and tokenized-stock routing (Robinhood Chain, Ondo, Arc), a B2B API franchise, Aqua as a new liquidity primitive whose fees accrue on-chain to the DAO, and team-fund accumulation. None of these yet shows up as holder cash flow.

### What would move the token

| Catalyst | Timing | Bullish if | Bearish if |

| --- | --- | --- | --- |

| Aqua Season 2 vote and start | temp check Nov 2026; start ≥2026-11-10 | DAO fee revenue rises toward incentive cost (gates at day 30/60) | volume stays at about $0.2–0.5M/day; incentives paid in 1INCH are sold |

| Degensoft "Development & Service Fee" proposal | announced in 1IP-103; date TBD | small, performance-linked, with vesting | large recurring outflow from a roughly $4.5M treasury |

| Resolver Access Fees / any fee switch to stakers or buyback | no date | a mechanism routing aggregator or Fusion value to the DAO or holders | continued "no fee sharing" stance |

| 1inch Card shutdown | 2026-12-18 | - | minor product retrenchment |

| Binance hack follow-through | ongoing | no further 1INCH dumps (hack wallet balance is now 0) | other stolen holdings or forced sellers |

| Large holder flows | any time | Team Fund buys | Team Fund, unlabeled whales or the 39.3M on Robinhood Chain moving to CEXs |

| Volume and market-share data | monthly | RWA/Robinhood/Solana flow reverses the volume decline | further share loss to CoW, Kyber, 0x and Uniswap |

| Bukov–1inch dispute | no date | clean resolution | litigation or equity conflict |

