### How it works

#### The product (what users actually touch)

- 0x Swap API (EVM): an off-chain router (the "Lightning" engine since 2026-11-02, ~80 ms median quote latency) that indexes 370+ liquidity sources on 17+ chains. It returns a ready-to-sign transaction that routes the user's trade across AMMs (Uniswap v2/v3/v4, Curve, Balancer, Aerodrome, etc.) and 0x's proprietary RFQ market makers [3][13][14].

- Settlement contracts ("0x Settler", since Swap API v2 in 2024): the user approves tokens to AllowanceHolder (0x0000000000001fF3684f28c67538d4D072C22734 on Cancun chains) or Permit2. The current Settler instance executes the route and enforces minimum output. Settler addresses rotate. The canonical ones are read from the ERC-721 registry/deployer 0x00000000000004533Fe15556B1E086BB1A72cEae via ownerOf(featureId): 2 = taker-submitted, 3 = meta-tx/gasless, 4 = intents, 5 = bridge [15]. The legacy v4 Exchange Proxy 0xDef1C0ded9bec7F1a1670819833240f027b25EfF still exists (limit/RFQ orders).

- Gasless API: 0x relays meta-transactions, so the user pays no native gas. Gas cost is deducted from the trade [3].

- Cross-Chain API: a bridge aggregator with 12 bridge providers behind one API; general availability on 2026-06-04 (per The Defiant, summarised on CMC [18][19]). Chain count and private-beta date not verified in a primary source.

- Swap API on Solana: the first non-EVM chain. Open beta since 2026-08-04, with zero swap fees as an introductory offer. Kamino and Titan route through it [14].

- Matcha (matcha.xyz): 0x Labs' own retail front end (swaps, limit orders, "Matcha Auto" gas-abstracted trading). Matcha Meta is a meta-aggregator that compares 0x against 1inch, Kyber, OKX and others [13].

#### The token (what ZRX actually does on-chain)

- Governance of the community treasury: ZrxTreasury (deployed 2021-04-16) holds 6.06M ZRX. Parameters read on-chain: proposal threshold 100,000 ZRX; quorum 10,000,000 ZRX; voting period 259,200 s (3 days). proposalCount() = 15. Event logs show 15 ProposalCreated and 10 ProposalExecuted events. The last proposal was created on 2024-06-04, the last vote cast on 2024-06-16, and the last proposal executed on 2023-12-24. There has been no on-chain treasury governance for about 29 months. Voting power comes from ZRX staked or delegated in ZrxVault.

- Protocol-upgrade governance: a separate system (ZeroExProtocolGovernor with wrapped ZRX "wZRX", 0xfcfaf7834f134f5146dbb3274bab9bed4bafa917, created 2023-04-06). wZRX totalSupply() = ~1,062 ZRX, so it is effectively unused. The Settler contracts that carry today's volume are owned and upgraded by 0x Labs (deployer owner 0xf36b9f50e59870a24f42f9ba43b2ad0a4b8f2f51), not by ZRX governance.

- Staking (v3 legacy): ZRX could be staked to market-maker pools (Staking Proxy V3 0xa26e80e7Dea86279c6d778D702Cc413E6CFfA777, 7-day epochs, current epoch 340). Rewards came from per-fill protocol fees in ETH. ZEIP-91 set the fee to $0 from 2021-09-29 as an "experiment" [11]. The v4 Exchange Proxy's getProtocolFeeMultiplier() returns 0 today (on-chain read). Stakers earn nothing. A 0x Labs staff member (forum user brentoshiro, 2022-10-13) wrote that even if staking were turned back on "there would be very few staking rewards to go around", because most liquidity comes from aggregated AMM sources and 0x Labs' RFQ system, "neither of which carry a protocol usage fee", and that "ZRX has always been a governance token" [11]. Forum threads from 2024–2025 show users struggling to unstake because the staking UI is broken, and they rely on Etherscan "write proxy" calls [11][12].

- Not present: no buyback, no burn, no fee switch, no ve-locking, no gas usage, no collateral role, no API discount for holding ZRX.

### Utility

- Real utility today: voting on the ~6M ZRX community treasury (dormant since 2024) and on hypothetical protocol upgrades via wZRX (unused). Legacy staking still functions mechanically but pays $0.

- Not needed for: using Swap/Cross-Chain/Gasless APIs (integrators pay 0x Labs in fees or subscriptions in USD or the traded tokens), trading on Matcha, paying gas, accessing RFQ liquidity, or Settler contract upgrades. AI agents pay $0.01 USDC per Swap API call via x402, not ZRX [19].

- Bottom line: ZRX is a governance-only token whose governance does not control the revenue-generating assets (APIs, Matcha, Settler), which are owned by 0x Labs.

### Why people buy and sell it

#### Demand drivers

- Optionality on a future fee switch or value link. Holders are betting that 0x Labs will eventually connect a business routing $64B/yr to the token. On 2021-12-17 the 0x DAO update said 0x Labs aimed "to share initial thoughts" on new network economics "in early 2022"; co-founder Will Warren replied on 2021-12-20 that "we must nail the economics" and that a formal proposal had been held off in 2021 [11]. No such proposal has appeared since.

- Narrative beta: "OG DeFi infra", AI-agent payments (x402), tokenised stocks and RWAs routing (Ondo, Centrifuge), Hyperliquid ecosystem (HyperEVM, Elysium) and Robinhood Chain. Moves are mostly in line with the market. A short-lived spike to $0.131 on 2026-10-11 retraced fully within a month [2].

- Exchange presence: still listed on Coinbase, Binance (ZRX/USDT spot and perps), Upbit and Bithumb (KRW pairs, historically a Korean retail token), and Bybit.

#### Supply / sell pressure

- No emissions or unlocks. The overhang is 151.6M ZRX in 0x-controlled wallets (Ext Dev Pool + Team Vesting, 17.9% of circulating-equivalent), which can be moved at 0x's discretion. They were last touched in 2021 and 2024 respectively.

- Large exchange inventories: Binance Cold Wallet 28 41.6M plus Binance Cold Wallet 20 18.0M, Bithumb 17.7M, and unlabeled 149.2M and 30.5M wallets with exchange-like patterns.

- Delistings shrink the buyer base: Bitfinex fully delisted ZRX (trading ceased 2025-11-27); Binance removed the ZRX/BTC margin pair (2025-12-04) and the ZRX/BTC spot pair no longer trades (Binance API status "BREAK" on 2026-11-10; spot removal date 2025-12-12 is from secondary reports, not verified); Phemex removed ZRX/USDT (2026-09-11, secondary source) [17][18].

- Holder fatigue: forum posts call the token "abandoned" (2025-01-07, 2025-11-26) [12].

### The protocol/business

What it does: B2B DEX-aggregation infrastructure. 0x sells "swap as a service" to wallets, exchanges, fintechs and trading bots, which embed swaps without building routing themselves. Self-reported totals: $200B+ volume settled, 211M+ transactions, 14M+ unique wallets, 500+ teams, 45M+ tokens indexed, 4.4% revert rate, 99.9%+ uptime [3]. DefiLlama's all-time count is lower at $151.7B, because it does not cover every period and chain [5].

Audience and integrators: Coinbase (Coinbase DEX trading in the main app from 2025; Base App swaps; "Swap API" inside Coinbase Developer Platform; 0x says it is "one of only two partners" at Coinbase scale), MetaMask, Phantom, Robinhood (Robinhood Wallet; day-one on Robinhood Chain, with $6.5B+ routed there per 0x), Farcaster wallet, Zora creator-coin routing, Kraken (per The Defiant, 2026-05-14 [16]), Kamino and Titan on Solana [13][14][16][20]. The user type is retail traders inside large consumer apps, which makes 0x a "white-label" layer that end users rarely see.

Where it is popular: volume by chain over 30 days (DefiLlama breakdown, to 2026-11-09): Ethereum $2.84B, Polygon $1.14B, Base $0.61B, Robinhood Chain $0.41B, BSC $0.38B, Arbitrum $0.28B, Monad $0.09B, Avalanche $0.06B, HyperEVM $0.05B, Solana $0.03B [5]. The company is US-based and SOC 2 certified [3].

Corporate structure: 0x Labs / ZeroEx Holdings, Inc. is a private, VC-funded company. It raised a $15M Series A (2021) and a $70M Series B led by Greylock (April 2022) [23]. It acquired Flood (flood.bid, routing team) in 2025 [13]. Headcount grew more than 40% in 2025 [13].

