### Current problems and risks

- Zero value accrual, with no plan. The company monetises (0.15% fee, subscriptions, Matcha) and the token does not. This has lasted more than 5 years since fees were set to $0 (2021-09-29). This is the core thesis risk.

- Governance is dormant and has no control. The last treasury vote was June 2024; wZRX protocol governance holds about 1,062 ZRX; Settler upgrades are owned by 0x Labs. ZRX holders cannot force a fee switch on the contracts that carry volume.

- Community attrition. Forum threads: "Why does the 0x Team Ignore ZRX?" (2025-01-07), "Unstaking: smoke and mirrors" (2025-02-22, broken staking UI and scam DMs), "Request: reinstating protocol fees" (2025-05-05), "Tokenomics" (2025-11-23: "we basically have been abandoned") [12].

- Liquidity erosion. Bitfinex delisting (2025-11-27), Binance ZRX/BTC and margin pairs removed (December 2025), Phemex delisting (2026-09-11). 45.4% of reported spot volume sits on Poloniex, a low-quality venue. Market cap is $73M.

- Insider overhang: 151.6M ZRX (15.2% of total supply) in 0x-controlled wallets with no lock.

- Security and brand: the SwapNet exploit (2026-01-25, $13.43M from 20 Matcha Meta users who had disabled One-Time Approval and granted direct allowances to SwapNet; one user lost about $13.34M of it). 0x's AllowanceHolder and Settler contracts were not affected [20].

- Leadership change: co-founder and co-CEO Will Warren left the role in May 2026 (stays on the board). No successor structure or restructuring was officially announced [16].

- Competition: Jupiter dominates Solana; KyberSwap, OKX, CoW, Uniswap's own routing and DFlow compete on EVM. Customer concentration in a few big wallets (Coinbase, MetaMask) means one lost contract could move share.

- What is going well (business, not token): 0x volume share rose from 6.8% (1y) to 9.4–10.7% (30d/24h). September 2026 was a record month at $10.3B. 0x has new chains (Monad, Plasma, Robinhood Chain, Arc, Elysium), RWA/stock routing, and Coinbase distribution. The business narrative is "neutral Stripe-like swap infrastructure for fintech and AI agents", but it accrues to 0x Labs equity.

### What would move the token

- Bullish: a 0x Labs or ZEIP proposal tying revenue to ZRX (fee share, buyback with API or Matcha revenue, a new staking model). A ProposalCreated event on ZrxTreasury, a forum post by 0x Labs staff on "network economics", or a token migration with value accrual would be first-order catalysts. Secondary: new top-tier listings, or a 0x Labs strategic event (acquisition or token-equity alignment) that addresses ZRX.

- Bearish: outflows from the Ext Dev Pool (0x206376e8…) or Team Vesting (0xDB63D40C…) wallets to exchanges; further delistings (especially Binance ZRX/USDT spot or perps, Coinbase, or Upbit/Bithumb warnings); explicit statements that 0x Labs' business is independent of ZRX; loss of a major integrator.

- Dated milestones known: none scheduled for the token. Product cadence: Solana Swap API GA (beta since 2026-08-04, date not announced); the "something new coming to the 0x stack" teaser (August 2026, unspecified) [19]. No unlocks remain.

- For Tank: 0x product launches (new chain, latency, RWA routing) have historically not translated into ZRX price because there is no value path. Treat them as low-signal for a long ZRX position unless they come with a tokenomics change.

